he\nbest measured form was restored before final verification.\n\nTests retain all 32 original pipeline cases and both original direct EX cases.\nAdded five pipeline cases covering writer priority, x0, independent sources,\nAUIPC/immediate overrides, forwarded stores, retained load WB during an older\nmemory hold, load-use/fetch-stall alignment, trap-suppressed writes (including\nfallback from suppressed EX to an older matching WB writer), and consumers\naccepted on blocking completion. Added direct EX coverage for all independent\nsource combinations and overrides, raw branch/store/RVFI operands, and DIV\noperand capture after forwarding writers drain. Existing MUL/JALR cap\n…[1209 of 4281 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ff36f41b1e3f109d]…\nedian 58.874 MHz;\n  option 0 uses 3,963 LUT4, 1,105 FF, 52 LUT-RAM, six BSRAM, two DSP.\n  Relative to 58.072 MHz and the same cycle count, this is a 1.38% improvement\n  and approximately 133.52 iterations/second. Critical paths moved from\n  destination tags to regfile data/branch recovery. Option 0's worst reported\n  arrival is 23.968 ns; options 1/2 report 22.280 ns.\n\nConcern: local vendor mapping does not reproduce the prototype's 61.748 MHz\nmedian or exceed the 4.6% fitness threshold. The implementation follows the\nrequested behavior and removes the EX tag comparison path, but placement and\n  mapping now leave the regfile/branch-recovery path limiting timing. Initial\nvector-enable/PC-first mapping measured 58.173 MHz median; placing bypass OR\nterms first measured 56.211 MHz median, so neither was selected. All final\ncorrectness gates completed successfully. Generated local logs are under\ncores/bench/generated/local_checks/ and are scratch artifacts, not deliverables.\nChanged tracked paths are all allowed.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
