{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Predecode and fuse fast execute result selection\n\nImplemented the hypothesis in core_pkg.sv, id_stage.sv, alu.sv and ex_stage.sv.\nID/EX now contains a 12-bit fast_result_sel and remains the same pipeline\nboundary. Decode registers one choice for ADD through LUI, link-only for\nJAL/JALR, and no fast choice for M operations. Reset, flush and bubbles clear\nthe field; decode holds retain it while the existing operand refresh runs.\n\nThe ALU exposes eleven independent 32-bit candidates in a packed output bank.\nIts binary output remains available for standalone use; the core does not\nconsume that output. Binary operations still drive the unchanged multiply and\ndivide units. EX uses the registered choices for its un-emitted arithmetic\nproducer and pending launch result. The capture bank qualifies choice bits\nwith fast_emit before masking each arithmetic/link word, then ORs those words\ndirectly with the held and completed sources. Other payload fields retain\ntheir input-valid guard. Forwarding keeps separate arithmetic/link sources,\nthe existing late qualification, EX-over-WB priority and retained-WB refresh.\n\nJALR targets use the independent ADD candidate with bit zero cleared, while\nthe registered pending record retains PC+4, original operands, successor,\ntarget/trap metadata and both prediction snapshots. No latency, predictor,\nhandshake, retirement-width, decoder, M-unit or branch-comparison changes.\n\nTests retain all existing assertions and adapt both packed ID/EX layouts to\n340 bits. Added 6,259 exact fast-operation cases, independent one-hot/binary\ndisagreement checks, effective bubble/reset/squash and held-result checks,\nwrapping jump links, and exact JALR pending-record assertions. All pipeline\ntests now check instruction/selector association each cycle. A new directed\nfull-RVFI ISS program covers every arithmetic choice, every shift amount,\nsigned boundaries, carries, LUI/AUIPC and immediates, dependent consumers,\nback-to-back changes, instruction stalls, long data stalls, recovery and\nboth direct and pending indirect link consumers. Existing random programs\ncontinue to run against the unchanged ISS with zero waits and both stalls.\n\nFinal-source checks completed: strict Verilator lint passed; all six pytest runners\npassed (133 cocotb cases); make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1 passed selftest in both stall\nmodes and stalled CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB validation. A separate canonical\nCoreMark IPC check reported exactly 4,483,027 bracketed cycles, 10 iterations.\nEarlier equivalent RTL forms passed fast formal 53/53 without failures or\ncounterexamples. Final-source fast formal is still running.\n\nTiming expression refinements preserve the same behavior. Earlier forms\nmeasured medians of 83.436 and 83.364 MHz, below the required 87.795 MHz.\nFinal source timing is pending. The main concern is\nplacement sensitivity and competing stall-to-ID operand capture paths;\nthe prototype's performance gain must not be assumed from correctness alone.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
