{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_76", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check\ngit status --short\ncat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_if_stage.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\nImplemented the requested predictor policy in rtl/if_stage.sv. The table has\nfour constant-generated banks, each with separate 32-row tag, target and\ncounter arrays. The seven-bit index is PC[8:2] XOR PC[15:9]; every row retains\nthe complete 23-bit PC[31:9] tag and 30 aligned target bits. Bank reads use\nfive-bit row indices and a balanced four-way bank selection.\n\nConditional misses allocate weakly taken only when taken. Matching branches\nkeep the original Boolean saturating transitions for either outcome. Jumps\nallocate strongly taken. Ineligible events invalidate only a matching valid\ntag. Skipped allocations gate both physical writes and the forwarded logical\nrow. Training snapshots include the complete row, including its target, and\nadjacent events forward only when all seven hashed index bits match.\n\nThe three fetch records, enqueue/dequeue priorities, accepted-MEM recovery,\ntraining capture/commit edges, reset behavior, execution, decoding and nret=1\nexternal ports retain their existing behavior. No other RTL file changed.\n\nImplementation refinements: updates write the registered event tag and target\ndirectly once allocation/update is qualified; these equal the logical\npost-update values. The full fetch-tag comparison uses kept two-bit equality\nleaves. Training tag/valid/counter snapshots have synthesis-preserve attributes\nto retain the existing register boundary. These changes do not add latency or\nchange direction/recovery policy.\n\nTests now model the full hash and taken-only policy. Coverage includes all\n128 indices, high tags/targets, skipped allocations and complete-row forwarding,\nfour-bank independence, true tag conflicts, saturation, eligibility failures,\nreset cancellation, training on recovery and 500 randomized adjacent events.\nPipeline tests retain the original exact transfer and immutable-snapshot checks\nand add a hot cross-bank loop with both bus holds and blocking MUL/DIV work.\n\nFinal validation: required Verilator lint passes without warnings; all seven\ncocotb runners pass, including all 52 pipeline tests. The unchanged formal\nsuite passes 53 checks, zero failures, on the final RTL. The initial formal\nrun also passed; zero formal fix attempts and no counterexamples occurred.\nThe unchanged ISS cosim passes selftest with and without stalls. Canonical\nCoreMark passes CRC, success UART, timing markers and OOB validation, and\nreconfirms 4,163,767 bracketed cycles. NRET=1 was explicitly supplied to make\ncosim/make fpga, matching the unchanged core.yaml.\n\nThe completed make fpga evaluation and independent vendor timing run both\nmeasure 88.379 / 85.308 / 85.308\nMHz for placement options 0 / 1 / 2: median 85.308 MHz. It reports 7,350 logic\ncells, 2,719 registers, 176 LUT RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs. The predictor\nis LUT RAM; the BSRAMs belong to the unchanged benchmark memory wrapper.\nThe measured median and cycles imply 204.88 iterations/sec, below 233.61.\nAcceptance would require Fmax above 97.269761 MHz at this cycle count.\n\nConcern: despite reducing the champion's timed cycles by 132,797 (3.09%),\nthe larger hashed lookup lowers vendor Fmax enough to regress fitness. The\nworst option-1 path is fetch-PC bit 10 through predictor lookup back to\nfetch-PC bit 28; accepted-MEM/training latency remains unchanged. This is\na correctly functioning, unsuccessful fitness hypothesis; no acceptance\nis claimed. All correctness/build gates pass; the fitness acceptance gate\nfails.\n\nCommands used: the requested verilator --lint-only invocation;\npytest -q cores/bench/test/;\nRTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh;\nNRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench;\npython3 -m tools.eval.gowin bench --all-options;\nNRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
