ted\n[30%] Placement Phase 2 completed\n[50%] Placement Phase 3 completed\nRunning routing......\n[60%] Routing Phase 0 completed\n[70%] Routing Phase 1 completed\nImplemented eight words per tagged BTB row in eight independent constant-offset\nbanks of 32 unreset word-register leaves, with local resettable validity and\nbalanced masked-OR reads. Replay enters only after accepted selected predictions,\nuses registered row/offset/full-target context, prefers accepted bus words, and\nretains the three fixed fetch records and ordinary immutable prediction snapshots.\n\nBus-only accepted fills and association invalidations apply one edge later.\nTraining ingress now s\n…[1135 of 4207 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:26f4ec17100c672e]…\nthat squashes an already captured younger instruction.\nThe initial binary-decoded payload organization measured only 39.804 MHz on\nplacement option 0 (13,989 logic cells, 11,351 registers). Its worst replay-selection\npath had 21.292 ns of routing versus 3.564 ns of logic. This routing cost motivated\nredundant registered row/offset one-hot decodes (40 bits) and moving offset masking\nto each constant word leaf, ahead of the balanced OR reductions. The required\nbinary five-bit row and three-bit offset and all replay semantics remain intact.\nFull unit tests, revalidation and median vendor timing of this final organization\nare still being completed. Main implementation\nconcerns are 8,192 additional instruction word bits and the resulting selection,\nfanout and routing cost. Fitness acceptance requires measured median Fmax above\n94.791795 MHz at the measured cycle count.\n\nThe Makefile cosim build defaults to NRET=2, so the authorized unchanged gate was\ninvoked with NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench to match core.yaml.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
