{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Isolate division in a bounded multicycle execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz and its reported worst path traverses\\nforwarding and the execute ALU across 156 cells. The ALU currently infers\\ncombinational signed and unsigned division and remainder networks, placing\\ndeep arithmetic behind the ordinary EX operand muxes and ahead of the\\nregistered result used for memory addresses and subsequent forwarding.\\nRemoving these networks from single-cycle execution offers much more\\ntiming headroom than a small improvement in instruction throughput. There\\nare no prior structural attempts or recorded lessons in this fixture.\\nSource inspection finds the visible divisions in CoreMark list sizing and\\ninitialization, before the measured iteration loop; its timed list,\\nmatrix, state, and CRC kernels therefore appear unlikely to pay a large\\ndynamic divide penalty. Confirm this with the unchanged bracketed cosim.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz and its reported worst path traverses\\nforwarding and the execute ALU across 156 cells. The ALU currently infers\\ncombinational signed and unsigned division and remainder networks, placing\\ndeep arithmetic behind the ordinary EX operand muxes and ahead of the\\nregistered result used for memory addresses and subsequent forwarding.\\nRemoving these networks from single-cycle execution offers much more\\ntiming headroom than a small improvement in instruction throughput. There\\nare no prior structural attempts or recorded lessons in this fixture.\\nSource inspection finds the visible divisions in CoreMark list sizing and\\ninitialization, before the measured iteration loop; its timed list,\\nmatrix, state, and CRC kernels therefore appear unlikely to pay a large\\ndynamic divide penalty. Confirm this with the unchanged bracketed cosim.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU with one shared, bounded multicycle\\nradix-2 restoring divider, le\n…[87088 of 90160 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:feb651f4af6532c0]…\n1, \"delta_pct\": 6.91, \"vs_baseline\": 899.17, \"fmax_mhz\": 48.238, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3983322, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3773, \"ff\": 1161, \"seeds\": [45.398, 48.238, 48.238], \"perturbations\": [[0, 45.398, 16], [1, 48.238, 15], [2, 48.238, 15]], \"lutram\": 52, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_addr_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -17.027, \"arrival_ns\": 27.322, \"logic_cells\": 19, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:33:19.208036Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-003-r3s2 (regression, +6.91%): A compact four-entry flow-through fetch FIFO overlaps load-use/dmem/divider holds with instruction-bus acceptance, but its gain lost to registering MUL/JALR (+16.27%), showing that fetch stall reduction can remain secondary to cutting EX timing cones.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
