{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_67", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r10s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r10s0',\n'title':'Use conditional EX/MEM capture instead of wide emission masks',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 187.23 at 83.934 MHz with 4,483,027 bracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh unchanged placement-1 run reproduced 83.934 MHz and found tightly competing EX/ALU-to-ID operand paths and branch-to-pending-payload paths. The r8s0 experiment removed EX's redundant input-valid mask and gained 4.45%, just below the 4.6% acceptance margin. EX/MEM still forms every one of its 295 payload bits through a held/completed/fast masked OR with an implicit all-zero bubble. This makes late emission controls part of the result capture datapath even when only validity and control fields need a bubble encoding.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Optimize EX/MEM payload storage as one local capture-control change. Replace the 295-bit emission-masked OR feeding the physical EX/MEM register with conditional capture of concrete payloads. Preserve the existing instruction latency, pipeline topology, forwarding, predictor policy, blocking units and nret=1 contract.\n\nKeep full synchronous reset clearing. A genuine older MEM stall holds the entire EX/MEM record, with the same priority as the existing held_emit term. When not stalled, accepted older recovery clears the entire EX/MEM record to zero. Otherwise capture completed_payload on completed_emit, capture payload on fast_emit, and on an ordinary non-emitting cycle clear only reg_q.valid and reg_q.ctrl, retaining the other data fields. No stale mem_read, mem_write or reg_write bit may survive a bubble. Reset, stall, recovery, completion and fast advancement must retain the original source priorities; an asserted stall and squash must still retain the older held record while canceling younger pending work. Recovery metadata must retain its current update semantics and cannot become live on an invalid record.\n\nRemove the separate in.valid mask around construction of the combinational fast/launch payload, as r8s0 did. Launch and fast_emit already require valid input. Keep every payload field correct for an emitted instruction and keep the existing source-specific producer eligibility, link selection, alignment traps and pending capture. Keep the effective next-state summary used by forwarding logically identical to the old fully zeroed reg_d expression: it is a producer description, not necessarily a literal copy of the retained invalid physical register. Producer write eligibility must continue to require validity or an actual emission; a bubble's retained rd/result must never suppress another forwarding source.\n\nThe intended timing gain comes from replacing wide data masking and implicit zero selection with a payload capture enable, combined with removing redundant input-valid masking. Ordinary invalid data is unobservable, while explicit zero control fields preserve the existing MEM/WB held-producer discipline. Do not change ID's bubble representation, reset or flush logic. Do not remove the held-operand repair network or register-file flops. This remains one EX capture micro_opt, with no extra execution cycle, new memory structure or changed predictor.\n\nAudit every consumer of the retained invalid EX/MEM payload: memory read/write enables, dmem hold detection, accepted MEM producer qualification, predictor training and recovery, retirement, and retained MEM/WB forwarding. All must retain their existing validity qualifications. On an ordinary bubble MEM/WB may capture stale data but must capture zero register-write control, so a later data-memory hold cannot expose a ghost WB producer. Preserve bounded accesses, exactly-once stores, strict RVFI order, original retiring operands and PCs, legality and alignment traps, and both real and ALTOPS RV32M arithmetic.\n\nRequire the unchanged unit, fast formal and stalled instruction cosim gates and canonical marker-bracketed CoreMark CRC/UART checks. Add directed coverage for a useful fast result followed by imem bubbles, long pending MUL/DIV/JALR sequences, same-destination consumers, memory holds, wrong-path memory operations and blocking launches, reset, and accepted recovery. Check no false producer, duplicate retirement, predictor training or memory effect from retained invalid payload. Preserve existing reset and recovery zero-bubble assertions; tests of ordinary invalid payload may inspect validity/control and externally observable behavior without requiring unused data bits to be zero.\n\nEstimate six percent higher fitness, with low confidence: capture-enable feedback, mapping choices and competing decode/predictor paths can limit the gain. CoreMark cycles should remain unchanged. Acceptance then requires median vendor Fmax above 87.795 MHz. Preliminary isolated arithmetic, operand-delivery and control probes did not exceed that threshold, so no accepted improvement is claimed. The implementation phase must judge median Gowin Fmax multiplied by measured iterations/cycle; the hypothesis must not be accepted on resource reduction or RVFI pruning alone.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the physical EX/MEM wide emission-masked OR with conditional completed/fast payload capture, genuine MEM hold, full reset/recovery clearing and validity/control-only ordinary bubbles. Remove the redundant input-valid payload mask. Preserve effective producer summaries, all hold/squash priorities, pending metadata, recovery and training behavior.'''.strip()},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'''Exercise nonzero records followed by ordinary bubbles, blocking launches/completion, genuine older MEM holds, simultaneous stall/squash, reset and accepted recovery. Retain all architectural and side-effect assertions and full reset/recovery zero-bubble checks; assert zero control and ineligibility for retained invalid records.'''.strip()},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Check retained invalid EX/MEM payload cannot cause a ghost producer, memory transaction, predictor update or retirement through imem stalls, memory waits, pending MUL/DIV/JALR, dependent consumers and recovery. Preserve exact RVFI results/operands/order, exactly-once stores and every hard-invariant check.'''.strip()}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=92,default_style=None))\nprint('Revised hypothesis file to the focused EX/MEM capture-control angle.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
