{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n    d = json.loads(line)\n    if d.get('category') == 'micro_opt':\n        print('\\\\nID:',d['id'],'TITLE:',d['title'])\n        print('fitness:',d.get('fitness'),'delta:',d.get('delta_pct'),'fmax:',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'cycles:',d.get('cycles'))\n        print('path:', d.get('critical_path'))\n        h = d.get('hypothesis', {})\n        if isinstance(h,dict):\n            print('hypothesis:',h.get('hypothesis',''))\n        print('notes:',d.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID: baseline-bench-847e570 TITLE: Baseline retest for cores/bench\nfitness: 12.12 delta: 0.0 fmax: 5.442 cycles: 4491485\npath: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhypothesis: \nnotes: \n\nID: hyp-20261002-001-r1s0 TITLE: Share a combinational non-restoring divider across DIV and REM\nfitness: 14.25 delta: 17.57 fmax: 6.402 cycles: 4491485\npath: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -159.323, 'arrival_ns': 169.618, 'logic_cells': 888, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_rf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhypothesis: Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with a single shared,\nfully combinational, explicitly unrolled radix-2 non-restoring unsigned\nquotient-and-remainder engine. Preserve the existing ALU interface,\nzero-cycle combinational latency, pipeline registers, bus stalls, and\nnret=1 retirement contract. This is an arithmetic implementation change,\nwith no multicycle execution, pipeline changes, or operation caching.\n\nFor DIV and REM, form 32-bit unsigned magnitudes using conditional\ntwo's-complement negation; DIVU and REMU use the original operands.\nStarting with a 33-bit partial remainder R=0, consume dividend bits\nfrom bit 31 down to bit 0 in 32 elaboration-time-unrolled steps. If the\nprevious R is negative, the next R is (R << 1) + dividend_bit + divisor;\notherwise it is (R << 1) + dividend_bit - divisor. Each quotient bit is\nthe inverse sign of the updated R. Use explicit 33-bit unsigned bit\nvectors and modulo-2^33 arithmetic; after each complete update R fits\nthe signed 33-bit range even though the intermediate shift can overflow.\nForm the shifted dividend-insertion term as the wiring concatenation\n{R[31:0], dividend_bit}, rather than an additional arithmetic operation.\nMaterialize the divisor and its 33-bit two's-complement negative once,\nthen select the addend with the prece\n…[48823 of 51895 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2abd9257ed7469cd]…\nerve the described\ncircuit and judge actual median vendor Fmax times bracketed throughput.\n\nThe scratch prototype is under cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe/\nr11_rf_control; generated artifacts are transient and deleted before\nevaluation, so implement from this description. Retain all existing\nchecks and every external port, full address, RVFI operand/successor,\nretirement order, decoder legality, alignment trap, real/ALTOPS RV32M\nresult and exactly-once memory transaction. Add cycle-by-cycle assertions\nthat registered word selects equal decoded source addresses and that\nregistered write-first matches equal the actual qualified WB comparison.\nExercise all register numbers, x0, simultaneous reads/writes, distinct\nsame-rd producer ages, long decoded/EX/MEM holds, departing WB writers,\nloads and traps, blocking completion, imem bubbles, reset and recovery.\nRequire unchanged formal, stalled instruction cosim, canonical CoreMark\nCRC/UART/marker checks and median vendor timing. No evaluation changes.\n\nnotes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
