{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r12s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-001-r12s0\ntitle: \"Isolate effective-address capture from general execute result selection\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.34 iterations/sec at median Gowin Fmax 95.961 MHz\n  and 4,296,564 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path\n  starts at complete ID/EX ALU operand flops and passes through the fast\n  ALU and execute selection to the data-memory address endpoint. The\n  r11 register-file probe exposes the same endpoint. The earlier r3s0\n  dedicated-address experiment improved fitness by 12.06 percent but lost\n  that round to a larger structural gain; the present core still routes\n  addresses through the general ALU result, jump-link selection, input\n  validity masking and held/completed/fast result selection. Those choices\n  are unnecessary for load/store addresses. Other micro_opt attempts that\n  broadly changed EX masks or result selection produced smaller or\n  inconsistent gains, so target only this concrete address cone.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give loads and stores a dedicated 32-bit effective-address sum and\n  physical EX/MEM address register at the existing execution boundary.\n  This is one local datapath specialization, preserving pipeline depth,\n  instruction latency, single issue, nret=1 and the memory handshake.\n\n  Compute the modulo-2^32 sum in.rs1_val + in.imm directly from the\n  complete, stable ID/EX flops. Capture it in a separate resettable\n  address bank on every nonreset edge without a genuine older MEM hold;\n  otherwise retain it. The data input and capture enable must not depend\n  on the ALU operation, in.valid, jump/link choice, pending result,\n  completion readiness or recovery. Address contents for nonmemory\n  records are unobservable when read/write enables are zero. Only the\n  companion EX/MEM valid/control fields authorize a transaction. A\n  redirect can invalidate younger metadata while the unused address\n  bank captures an arbitrary sum; it cannot cause a memory side effect.\n\n  Add an effective_addr field to ex_mem_t and overlay t\n…[2840 of 5912 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b1253d6a65e1b9d3]…\neneral result selection\n      and pending completion. Export it in effective_addr while preserving\n      the original next-state, forwarding, recovery and training logic.\n      Update hard-coded packed widths safely for the expanded bundle.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Route all address consumers through effective_addr: bus address,\n      alignment, masks, extraction and RVFI aligned address. Preserve\n      transaction qualification, store/load data handling and writeback.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt packed EX/MEM width checks and verify independent address\n      capture, reset and genuine memory holds, keeping all result,\n      recovery, blocking-completion and invalid-input assertions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add exact address and memory-effect checks for forwarded operands,\n      offset carries, every lane, traps, long stalls, invalid records,\n      blocking completion and redirects; retain all architectural checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
