{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"agent_message","text":"The replicated bank preserves CoreMark’s CRCs and cycle count, but its median Fmax falls to 90.862 MHz, so I’m discarding it too. I’m now testing two smaller ALU simplifications: shared logical/arithmetic right-shift logic, and shared subtraction/less-than logic. The final YAML will select one angle."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_73", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r13s0.yaml')\nx={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r13s0',\n 'title':'Share right-shift data with parallel arithmetic sign fill',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 223.34 iterations/sec at median Gowin Fmax 95.961 MHz and 4,296,564 bracketed CoreMark cycles. An untouched placement-0 rebuild reproduced 88.343 MHz and the 16.618 ns operand-to-ALU-to-data-memory path. Prior wide one-hot result selection regressed 7.21 percent, and arithmetic moved before operand capture regressed 22.57 percent. Local probes also rejected a carry-prefix ALU and duplicated shifter operands. The remaining promising local angle is to reduce the right-shift cone itself without changing operand capture, result selection or stage latency.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Implement SRL and SRA using one shared 32-bit logical barrel shifter and a parallel sign-fill mask, entirely after the existing complete ID/EX operand registers. Preserve the binary ALU operation interface, pipeline boundaries, instruction cycles, predictor policy, forwarding sources, memory handshakes and nret=1.\n\nCompute right_logical = a >> b[4:0] and right_keep = 32'hffffffff >> b[4:0]. Form right_value = right_logical OR ((NOT right_keep) AND replicated(op == ALU_SRA AND a[31])). Select this same right_value for both ALU_SRL and ALU_SRA in the existing operation case. The constant all-ones mask is a small decode function of the shift amount; it must not become another word-wide variable-data shifter. Keep SLL, all ADD/SUB/logic/compare/LUI expressions, jump-link and EX emission selection, and the real and ALTOPS multiplier/divider unchanged. Do not introduce bit reversal, new operand registers, a pre-ID/EX partial shift, or one-hot operation flops.\n\nThe logical shifted data and sign-fill decode run in parallel, eliminating duplicate right-shift data routing and making arithmetic extension explicit at the output. This targets LUT use and routing on a timed fast-ALU cone with zero cycle penalty. Gowin may already share the original shifts or a competing RF/load-return path may limit the benefit; inspect the mapped resources and all placement options before crediting a gain.\n\nRetain all existing exact-bit arithmetic and handshake checks. Exercise SRL/SRA for every shift amount 0 through 31, high non-shamt bits in b, zero/all-ones/alternating/walking-bit a, signed extrema, and deterministic random operands. Verify the logical operation never receives sign fill, arithmetic zero-shifts preserve a, and shifting negative a by 31 yields all ones. Exercise dependent shifts feeding ALU, loads/stores, comparisons and branches through bus holds, recovery and blocking completion, preserving exact RVFI operands/results/order, traps and exactly-once memory effects.\n\nRequire unchanged formal and stalled instruction cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB and timing-marker validation, unchanged bracketed cycles, and median vendor Fmax across all three placement options. At unchanged cycles acceptance requires Fmax above 100.375206 MHz and fitness above 233.61364. This is a proposed local circuit change; no accepted timing improvement has been established.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Replace separate logical/arithmetic right-shift expressions with one shared logical shift and a parallel constant-mask sign-fill path. Keep original ports, binary operation case, SLL and all other RV32I results and clocked real/ALTOPS RV32M units unchanged.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Extend exact SRL/SRA checks across every shamt, signed boundaries, structured and deterministic random words, and ignored upper bits of b. Retain every existing fast-ALU and exact real RV32M result/handshake assertion.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add dependent right-shift consumers through load/store addressing, arithmetic and branches under bus stalls, held operands, recovery and blocking completion. Retain all original architectural, RVFI order, trap and side-effect checks.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
