{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_98", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil,yaml,json,jsonschema\nroot=Path('cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe');rtl=root/'bidirectional';rtl.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nfor p in (root/'rightsigned').glob('*.sv'):shutil.copy2(p,rtl/p.name)\np=rtl/'alu.sv';s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('  wire signed [32:0] right_input = {(op == ALU_SRA) && a[31],a};','''  wire [31:0] reversed_a;\n  wire [31:0] reversed_result;\n  wire shift_left = op == ALU_SLL;\n  for (genvar i=0;i<32;i++) begin : g_reverse\n    assign reversed_a[i]=a[31-i];\n    assign reversed_result[i]=right_shifted[31-i];\n  end\n  wire [31:0] shift_input = shift_left ? reversed_a : a;\n  wire signed [32:0] right_input = {(op == ALU_SRA) && a[31],shift_input};''')\ns=s.replace('ALU_SLL:    out = a << shamt;','ALU_SLL:    out = reversed_result;')\ns=s.replace('    shamt = b[4:0];','    shamt = b[4:0];')\n# The old shamt signal now feeds no expression; remove it to keep lint clean.\ns=s.replace('  logic [4:0] shamt;\\\\n','').replace('    shamt = b[4:0];\\\\n','')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r13s0.yaml')\nx=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nx['title']='Share SRL and SRA through one explicitly sign-controlled barrel shifter'\nx['hypothesis']='''Implement SRL and SRA with one 33-bit signed right barrel shifter whose extension bit is selected from the registered operation. Keep the original complete ID/EX operand registers, pipeline boundaries, operation latency, binary ALU interface, forwarding, predictor policy, memory handshakes and nret=1.\n\nDefine a signed 33-bit wire right_input = {(op == ALU_SRA) && a[31], a}. Define a signed 33-bit wire right_shifted = right_input >>> b[4:0]. Both ALU_SRL and ALU_SRA select right_shifted[31:0] from the original operation case. A forced zero extension bit makes unsigned a positive at width 33, so SRL zero-fills even when a[31] is set. Copying a[31] into the extension bit makes SRA sign-fill. Zero shifts return a, and only b[4:0] affects the shift. Explicitly declare both wires signed; a concatenation alone is unsigned in SystemVerilog.\n\nThis shares the variable-data shift cone and its result selection while moving the logical/arithmetic distinction to a single extension-bit control. It should reduce duplicate routing and per-bit shift-result muxing at unchanged cycles. Keep SLL and every ADD/SUB/logic/compare/LUI result unchanged. Keep EX jump-link and emission selection and both real/ALTOPS clocked RV32M units unchanged. Do not add operand flops, stages, bit reversal, masks after the shared output, or one-hot operation fields. Gowin can remap common expressions and RF/load-return timing competes with EX, so improvement requires the measured median, not a single favorable placement.\n\nAn isolated Yosys SAT miter has proved this candidate's complete combinational fast-ALU output equivalent to the original for every op, a and b. This is a datapath-equivalence proof, not a replacement for the unchanged pipeline/formal gates or vendor timing. Earlier carry-prefix and operand-replication probes regressed; a parallel constant sign-mask right-shift implementation improved placement 0 but regressed the three-option median, so it is not this proposed circuit.\n\nRetain all existing tests and add exact SRL/SRA checks for every shift amount, high non-shamt bits in b, zero/all-ones/alternating/walking-bit operands, signed extrema and deterministic random values. Exercise shift-dependent ALU, memory-address, comparison and branch consumers through bus stalls, held operands, reset/recovery and blocking completion. Preserve exact RVFI operands/results/order, illegal/trap behavior and exactly-once memory side effects. Require unchanged formal, stalled ISS cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB/marker checks. At unchanged 4,296,564 bracketed cycles acceptance requires all-option median Fmax above 100.375206 MHz and fitness above 233.61364. No accepted timing improvement is claimed.'''\nx['changes'][0]['description']='Implement SRL/SRA with one explicitly signed 33-bit >>> network, selecting zero or a[31] for its extension bit from the binary operation and selecting the low 32 output bits for both operations. Keep ports, latency, SLL, all other fast results and real/ALTOPS M units unchanged.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=88));jsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated valid hypothesis to the compact sign-controlled right shifter')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
