{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_104", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil,yaml,json,jsonschema\nroot=Path('cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe');rtl=root/'branchbytes';rtl.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nfor p in Path('cores/bench/rtl').glob('*.sv'):shutil.copy2(p,rtl/p.name)\np=rtl/'ex_stage.sv';s=p.read_text()\nnetwork='''  wire [3:0] byte_eq, byte_lt;\n  for (genvar i=0;i<4;i++) begin : g_compare_byte\n    assign byte_eq[i] = in.rs1_val[i*8 +: 8] == in.rs2_val[i*8 +: 8];\n    assign byte_lt[i] = in.rs1_val[i*8 +: 8] < in.rs2_val[i*8 +: 8];\n  end\n  wire low_lt = byte_lt[1] || (byte_eq[1] && byte_lt[0]);\n  wire high_lt = byte_lt[3] || (byte_eq[3] && byte_lt[2]);\n  wire unsigned_lt = high_lt || ((byte_eq[3] && byte_eq[2]) && low_lt);\n  wire signed_lt = (in.rs1_val[31] \"'!= in.rs2_val[31]) ? in.rs1_val[31] : unsigned_lt;\n  wire equal_word = &byte_eq;\n'\"'''\ns=s.replace('  logic branch_cond, branch_taken, misalign_fault;',network+'\\\\n  logic branch_cond, branch_taken, misalign_fault;')\ns=s.replace('branch_cond = in.rs1_val == in.rs2_val;','branch_cond = equal_word;')\ns=s.replace('branch_cond = in.rs1_val \"'!= in.rs2_val;'\"','branch_cond = \"'!equal_word;'\"')\ns=s.replace('branch_cond = \"'$signed(in.rs1_val) < $signed(in.rs2_val);'\"','branch_cond = signed_lt;')\ns=s.replace('branch_cond = \"'$signed(in.rs1_val) >= $signed(in.rs2_val);'\"','branch_cond = \"'!signed_lt;'\"')\ns=s.replace('branch_cond = in.rs1_val < in.rs2_val;','branch_cond = unsigned_lt;')\ns=s.replace('branch_cond = in.rs1_val >= in.rs2_val;','branch_cond = \"'!unsigned_lt;'\"')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r13s0.yaml')\nx={'id':'hyp-20261002-001-r13s0','title':'Balance branch comparisons with parallel byte relation summaries','category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 223.34 iterations/sec at median Fmax 95.961 MHz with 4,296,564 bracketed CoreMark cycles. An untouched placement-0 rebuild reproduces 88.343 MHz. Its five worst paths include a 16.574 ns, 37-cell path from registered rs2 bit zero through EX into the pending next-PC register, alongside the ALU and operand-capture paths. Local carry-prefix, duplicated shifter-bank and several shared right-shifter probes failed to improve the three-option median. Branch comparisons still use wide signed/unsigned relational operators; a balanced comparison can shorten their carry-dependent resolution without moving arithmetic onto the memory-return path.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the EX branch relation datapath with four parallel eight-bit unsigned comparisons and a balanced two-level combination of equality/less-than summaries. This is a local branch-comparator micro_opt, preserving the pipeline, predictor, issue/retirement width and every instruction latency.\n\nFor bytes i=0..3 compute eq[i] = rs1[8*i +: 8] == rs2[8*i +: 8] and lt[i] = rs1[8*i +: 8] < rs2[8*i +: 8]. Byte 3 is most significant. Form low_lt = lt[1] OR (eq[1] AND lt[0]) and high_lt = lt[3] OR (eq[3] AND lt[2]) in parallel. Then unsigned_lt = high_lt OR (eq[3] AND eq[2] AND low_lt). Form signed_lt = (rs1[31] \"'!= rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_lt, and equal_word = AND-reduction(eq). BEQ/BNE use equal_word and its inverse; BLT/BGE use signed_lt and its inverse; BLTU/BGEU use unsigned_lt and its inverse. Preserve the branch-op default false. Use explicit fixed-width slices and this balanced grouping, not a serial byte-priority chain or a newly inferred 32-bit subtraction.\n\nAll inputs remain the original complete registered EX rs1_val/rs2_val. The comparator feeds the existing branch_cond, branch_taken, target/trap qualification, resolved next-PC and registered recovery exactly where the original comparator did. Preserve legal control-target alignment traps, jump/JALR handling, launch/consume priorities, pending instruction metadata and prediction snapshots, exactly-once accepted-MEM recovery/training, genuine memory holds and dominant squash/reset. Do not resolve branches in an earlier stage or add an extra resolution cycle. Keep the ALU, register file, forwarding, load extraction, fetch queue and predictor policy unchanged, including both real and ALTOPS RV32M arithmetic. Keep nret=1 and every top-level port and RVFI field.\n\nThe four independent narrow carry chains followed by two relation-combine levels should shorten signed/unsigned branch resolution and reduce duplicated comparison logic. Equality is shared across all branch functions. This trades a small amount of local logic for less serial comparator depth; Gowin remapping, routing and the competing ALU/RF/load-return paths remain uncertainties. Expect a six-percent timing-driven fitness gain with unchanged bracketed cycles and low confidence until full vendor evaluation. No accepted improvement is claimed. At unchanged cycles the required median Fmax is above 100.375206 MHz and fitness above 233.61364.\n\nRetain every correctness check. Add exact tests for all six branch functions with equal operands, every byte position as the highest differing byte, lower-byte differences that oppose the higher-byte relation, unsigned high-bit operands, signed extrema and deterministic random pairs. Test true and false outcomes, original prediction snapshots, aligned/misaligned targets, back-to-back resolving branches, load/ALU-produced operands, long bus holds, blocking completion and accepted older recovery. Check exact successors, traps, RVFI operands and contiguous order, and no younger side effects. Require unchanged formal, stalled ISS cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB/marker validation before all three Gowin placement options. Verify actual comparator structure/resources and use median Fmax times measured iterations/cycle, not an isolated placement or RVFI-only improvement.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace wide EX branch relational/equality expressions with four fixed eight-bit relation summaries, a balanced two-level unsigned less-than reduction, a sign-bit correction and shared equality. Keep all existing branch-op selection, targets/traps, pending payloads, emissions, recovery/training timing and other execution logic unchanged.'},{'file':'test/test_ex_stage.py','description':'Add exact six-function branch vectors covering highest differing bytes, opposing lower-byte relations, equality and signed/unsigned extrema, plus deterministic random operands. Preserve all current payload, trap, misalignment, prediction, hold/reset/squash, pending-completion and producer checks.'},{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Exercise the balanced comparator with forwarded ALU/load operands, adjacent branches, bus holds, blocking completion, predictor hits/misses and dominant accepted-MEM recovery. Preserve exact RVFI results/operands/successors/order and exactly-once memory side effects.'}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=88));jsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final focused branch-comparator hypothesis written and validated')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
