{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Predecode load lanes and flatten the memory return result mux\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.34 iterations/sec at median Gowin Fmax\n  95.961 MHz and 4,296,564 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent attempts\n  repeatedly exposed competing operand-delivery limits: r12s0 ended on\n  a 17.317 ns data-memory-to-ID/EX path, and moving arithmetic ahead\n  of operand capture in r12s1 made that return path 22.22 ns. The\n  existing MEM datapath performs lane extraction, sign/zero extension,\n  load-versus-ALU selection, then forwarding. No prior micro_opt has\n  directly specialized this load-return chain. Keep arithmetic behind\n  complete operand flops and optimize the existing memory formatter.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the generic shifted-word load formatter followed by a\n  load/ALU mux with registered one-hot lane controls and a single\n  factored result network. This is a local memory-return datapath\n  micro-optimization, with the current pipeline, predictor, register\n  file, arithmetic units and every instruction latency preserved.\n\n  Add an internal return-selector record to EX/MEM: four byte-lane\n  selects, two aligned halfword selects, a word select, an ALU select,\n  and byte/halfword sign-fill enables. Derive them from the same\n  instruction's mem_to_reg, mem_width, mem_sext and effective address\n  low bits, before the existing EX/MEM edge. The EX effective address\n  is the original ALU result, not the PC/link result. Carry these bits\n  with their instruction through exactly the existing fast, held and\n  pending-completion update priorities; reset and squash clear them.\n  Do not introduce a new stage, speculative acceptance or address\n  truncation. Unsupported/misaligned return cases may produce arbitrary\n  internal result bits only when the existing trap logic suppresses\n  architectural writes; retain all current alignment traps and bus gates.\n\n  In MEM, use fixed byte and halfword slices of dmem_rdata instead of\n  shifting a 32-bit word. Compute each output r\n…[3059 of 6131 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0fec03c2a84efdbe]…\nap and recovery priorities; replace\n      hard-coded packed-bundle replication widths with $bits(ex_mem_t).\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace variable load shifting and serial extension/load-ALU\n      selection with fixed slices and a factored masked-OR final result.\n      Reuse it for accepted forwarding and WB capture while preserving\n      load/read/raw RVFI data, alignment checking and all memory effects.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Check exact return-selector association for all legal load widths\n      and offsets through advance, hold, pending completion, bubbles,\n      reset and squash while retaining every existing assertion.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add lane/sign-boundary and unselected-byte perturbation cases,\n      dependent load consumers and same-rd writers under both bus stalls.\n      Preserve exact RVFI, alignment traps, masks, order, recovery,\n      blocking completion and exactly-once memory-effect checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
