{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_71", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Remove redundant bus qualification from decode source-tag matching\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.34 iterations/sec at median Gowin Fmax\n  95.961 MHz and 4,296,564 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent r13s0\n  and r13s2 timing reports repeatedly expose dmemReady-to-ID operand\n  controls. A local load-return predecode probe also shifted the worst\n  path to dmemReady-to-decoded provenance and fell to 90.593 MHz.\n  The current next-EX tag mux and next-MEM destination matches include\n  hold/emission controls even though id_stage samples these tags only\n  while replacing decoded_q, when those holds are necessarily absent.\n  Removing this redundant qualification targets the control cone itself.\nhypothesis: |\n  Simplify only source-tag matching for a replacing decoded record,\n  using the existing capture predicate to establish which producer\n  positions can actually be sampled. This is one local control-logic\n  micro_opt: retain every pipeline register, instruction latency,\n  operand data mux, arithmetic unit, memory formatter, predictor and\n  accepted-transfer control. Do not implement the unsuccessful\n  load-return probe or the broad early-RF/persistent-result repartition\n  from r13s1.\n\n  A decoded record is replaced only when !reset && !redirect &&\n  !stall_id, with stall_id = hold_ex || load_use_hazard. Thus replacement\n  implies !hold_ex, !dmem_stall, !execute_busy and no load-use flush.\n  The next EX instruction on every such edge is exactly decoded_w,\n  never the held id_ex_w alternative. Feed the source-tag comparisons\n  directly with decoded_w.rd and decoded_w.valid &&\n  decoded_w.ctrl.reg_write, eliminating hold_ex/flush/reset selection\n  from this matching datapath. Preserve nonzero-rd qualification and\n  compare both incoming raw source fields independently. Outside\n  replacement cycles these capture-only tags need not describe effective\n  next state, because id_stage does not sample them. Keep any separately\n  observable effective next-state produ\n…[4134 of 7206 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a0e9bd68f758e3c6]…\ncovery and\n      training expression and register priority.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Document and maintain the exact reset/squash/replace/hold sampling\n      domain of source-tag inputs. Keep the replacement and held-record\n      provenance update behavior and complete operand storage unchanged.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add replacement-edge equivalence assertions against the original\n      emission-qualified matches and actual next EX/MEM writer tags.\n      Retain held-record rebasing and all RVFI/order/side-effect checks;\n      cover loads, same-rd ages, blocking completion, arbitrary bus\n      holds, reset, recovery and disappearing WB.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Assert capture-only pending ownership equals actual registered\n      pending state across launches, incomplete/held completion,\n      consumption, reset and squash. Preserve all existing effective\n      producer, bubble, payload, trap and completion assertions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
