{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_83", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r14s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Factor operand-capture controls using registered producer ownership\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.34 iterations/sec at median Gowin Fmax\n  95.961 MHz and 4,296,564 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent r13s0\n  and r13s2 reports expose dmemReady-to-ID controls. Source-tag matching\n  and wide operand masks currently repeat acceptance qualifications\n  that are already enforced by the decoded and operand-bank capture\n  enables. A source-tag-only probe passed simulation but reached only\n  94.592 MHz, exposing load-return and branch paths. Apply the same\n  capture-domain simplification consistently to provenance and bypass\n  controls, without changing register boundaries or adding RF snapshots.\nhypothesis: |\n  Factor transfer qualification out of the capture-only source-tag and\n  operand-selection networks. Use registered producer ownership to\n  choose candidate values, and preserve the existing bank enables as\n  the sole authority to accept those values. This is one local control\n  micro_opt, with identical pipeline topology, instruction latency,\n  complete operand flops, arithmetic, memory formatting, register file,\n  frontend and predictor behavior.\n\n  A decoded record is replaced only when !reset && !redirect &&\n  !stall_id. Since stall_id = hold_ex || load_use_hazard, replacement\n  implies !hold_ex, !dmem_stall, !execute_busy and no load-use flush.\n  Thus the next EX instruction on every replacing edge is decoded_w.\n  Feed its source-tag comparisons directly with decoded_w.rd and\n  decoded_w.valid && decoded_w.ctrl.reg_write, eliminating the\n  hold_ex/flush/reset mux from this capture-only tag. Outside replacing\n  edges this tag is not sampled. Keep independently used effective\n  next-state producer summaries accurate.\n\n  Expose pending_q from ex_stage as an internal registered ownership\n  bit. For incoming next-MEM provenance compare both raw source fields\n  independently with the normal id_ex_w destination and the pending\n  ex_completed destination. Q\n…[5285 of 8357 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8335ceae796dfc37]…\nrces, registered age\n      priority, trap/load suppression, x0, RF fallback and complete\n      PC/immediate operand selection.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Document capture-only matching and candidate-value semantics.\n      Preserve reset/squash/replace/hold domains, held provenance\n      rebasing and reset/flush/hold/valid operand-bank priorities.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add decode-replacement and valid-operand-acceptance equivalence\n      against the original transfer-qualified selection. Preserve all\n      held-record, immutable-EX, RVFI/order and side-effect assertions;\n      cover same-rd ages, loads/traps, pending completion, bus waits,\n      departing WB, reset and accepted recovery.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Assert ownership equals registered pending state through launch,\n      held completion, consume, reset and squash. Retain every existing\n      effective-producer, zero-bubble, payload, trap and completion check.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
