{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_41", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261002-001-r15s0\ntitle: \\\"Prequalify and fuse register-file write-first operand forwarding\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.34 at 95.961 MHz with 4,296,564 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. Recent timing repeatedly exposes memory-readiness\n  qualification and MEM load-return selection before operand capture.\n  The asynchronous RF also puts a write-first mux before forwarding.\n  r11s0's registered RF read controls gained 5.22 percent on an older\n  frontend but lost its slot. r13s1 combined persistent routing with\n  a larger pipeline rewrite; r14s1's synchronous RAM integration lost.\n  Keep the champion's flop-bank storage and all pipeline boundaries.\n\n  A control-only prototype removes transfer events from operand data\n  selection and matches concrete producer tags on decoded acceptance.\n  It passes all 51 existing pipeline cases, eight unchanged ISS cosims\n  and canonical stalled CoreMark at exactly 4,296,564 bracketed cycles.\n  Median Gowin Fmax is 96.490 MHz versus the reproduced 95.961 MHz\n  champion, only 0.55 percent higher and below acceptance. The complete\n  proposal also removes serial RF write-first selection in that same\n  operand network. An EX-registered load-format probe measured only\n  87.205 MHz and is excluded.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace serial RF write-first selection followed by forwarding with\n  one operand network whose RF read controls are registered at the\n  existing decoded boundary. This is one operand-selection micro_opt.\n  Preserve all stages and instruction latencies, complete EX operand\n  flops, the asynchronous resettable RF word banks, ALU and predictor.\n  Add no synchronous read, LSU lane or precomputed arithmetic.\n\n  Register 31 nonzero RF word selects per source when the fixed fetch\n  head is accepted into decoded_q. These are genuine flops driven by\n  incoming instruction bits, not decodes of decoded_q's source fields.\n  Reset/squash clears them; valid replacement captures its selections;\n  invalid replacement captures zero; decoded holds retain them. Feed\n  the existing balanced constant-index read-tree leaves directly from\n  these vectors. Keep full register indices, synchronous writes and x0.\n\n  Register each decoded source's exact match to the WB instruction that\n  will exist next cycle. Its candidate is the current MEM instruction\n  with final trap-qualified writer intent and actual MEM/WB acceptance.\n  On replacement compare its rd to the incoming head's source; on a\n  hold compare to the held decoded source. Require valid ownership and\n  nonzero rd. Refresh both match bits on EVERY edge, including decoded\n  holds. A dmem hold invalidates next WB and clears the matches; reset\n  and accepted recovery clear source association. After each edge the\n  bits must equal actual qualified WB/source equality. Never retain a\n  match to a departed WB writer.\n\n  Expose raw balanced RF tree words separately from legacy write-first\n  outputs. Pass the raw words and registered WB word/matches directly\n  into forward_unit. Use one final disjoint masked-OR network for both\n  resolved RVFI operands and complete ALU operands: qualified youngest\n  EX, then qualified MEM, then matched WB, then raw RF; x0 yields zero.\n  Fold PC/immediate selection into that network as today. No raw RF word\n  should first traverse a WB data mux. Preserve a default legacy binary\n  address/write-first mode for standalone RF tests; core explicitly\n  enables predecoded read controls.\n\n  Use instruction ownership instead of transfer events in data masks.\n  Fast ownership requires valid nonblocking EX work and no pending\n  instruction; direct-jump ownership chooses its link. Completed-source\n  ownership requires pending_q and the captured trap-qualified payload.\n  MEM ownership uses its current valid, trap-qualified producer. Remove\n  fast_emit/link_emit/completed_emit and wb_accept from data masks while\n  retaining operation-kind, writer, registered source provenance, x0\n  and final trap qualification. Keep independent older matches so a\n  suppressed trapping writer exposes the correct older value. A youngest\n  unavailable load or blocking result must never be accepted through\n  an older-source fallback.\n\n  Leave transfer events unchanged for requests, consume, actual EX/MEM\n  movement, MEM acceptance, training, retirement and physical writes.\n  Keep them controlling the existing complete operand hold/flush bank.\n  During dmem waits or incomplete M results data may be transient, but\n  capture remains inhibited; reset and recovery clear the bank. Prove\n  value equivalence at operand acceptance, including completion followed\n  immediately by a different producer and simultaneous older recovery.\n\n  For replacing decoded provenance compare the incoming source directly\n  with the current decoded writer that will enter EX, before the late\n  hold-dependent next-tag mux. Match MEM candidates separately against\n  concrete fast and pending destinations. Capture through the unchanged\n  decoded acceptance only: when capture is possible MEM is not held and\n  pending work is complete. Held MEM cannot accompany new decode capture.\n  Preserve all original provenance rebasing during holds. Keep diagnostic\n  effective-next tags if tests use them, without putting their late mux\n  back into matching.\n\n  Preserve nret=1, every external port, full address, decoder/SYSTEM\n  legality, alignment trap, real and ALTOPS M result, exact RVFI fields,\n  contiguous order and exactly-once memory effects. Check registered\n  word selects and WB matches cycle by cycle against independent binary\n  comparisons. Cover all RF words, x0, same-rd producer ages, trapping\n  fallback, WB draining during holds, loads and blocking completions,\n  bus stalls, recovery and reset. Require unchanged unit, formal,\n  stalled ISS and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB/marker gates.\n\n  The final proposal is the complete prequalified and fused network,\n  not the measured control-only component. Estimate seven percent higher\n  fitness at unchanged cycles, with low confidence pending full vendor\n  timing. Acceptance requires median Fmax above 100.375206 MHz and\n  fitness above 233.61364 at these cycles. Final mux fanout, registered\n  read-select placement and competing EX/load-return paths can cap gains;\n  use all three vendor placements and actual bracketed throughput.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: |\n      Add integrated predecoded read controls and raw balanced-tree\n      outputs, preserving word flops, writes, reset and x0. Retain legacy\n      standalone binary/write-first behavior. Integrated raw words bypass\n      the old RF write-first data mux.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture genuine one-hot RF word selects at decoded acceptance with\n      exact reset/squash/replace/hold association. Compare incoming EX\n      provenance against concrete decoded writer fields before late hold\n      selection, preserving complete operand capture and hold rebasing.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Expose mutually exclusive fast, link and pending-result ownership\n      without readiness/consume gates. Preserve writer/trap qualification\n      and every emission, request, completion, hold and recovery rule.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire raw RF and WB candidates and registered read selects into the\n      unified network. Refresh exact next-WB/source match flops every\n      edge. Match concrete fast/pending MEM candidates before transfer\n      controls, retaining actual events and all capture interlocks.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Fuse EX/MEM/WB/raw-RF selection for raw and complete ALU operands\n      into disjoint masked ORs. Use ownership in data masks, retaining\n      age priority, final traps, independent fallback, x0 and PC/immediate.\n  - file: test/test_reg_file.py\n    description: |\n      Retain legacy tests and check integrated predecoded/raw reads\n      against an independent architectural register model, including\n      every word index, reset, x0 and simultaneous reads/writes.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Assert exact registered word/WB matches and acceptance-boundary\n      operands. Cover older WB draining during holds, same-rd age priority,\n      trap fallback, loads/M completion, stalls, recovery and reset.\n      Preserve all existing operand, order, trap and side-effect checks.\nYAML\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np='cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml'\nh=yaml.safe_load(open(p));jsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Schema valid:',h['id'],h['category'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
