{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_46", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261002-001-r15s0\ntitle: \\\"Qualify execute payload and operand forwarding once at capture\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.34 at 95.961 MHz with 4,296,564 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. Recent paths repeatedly cross dmem readiness,\n  producer qualification and wide operand capture. EX currently zeros\n  every payload word with in.valid before masking it again with\n  fast_emit; forwarding also gates words with transfer events even\n  when those same events already inhibit operand capture. r8s0's\n  validity-mask removal gained 4.45 percent on an older champion,\n  narrowly below acceptance. r13s1 bundled persistent routing with\n  RF snapshots and an LSU lane and regressed. Isolate the redundant\n  control qualification here, preserving every pipeline boundary.\n\n  A control-only prototype passes all 51 existing pipeline cases,\n  eight unchanged ISS cosims and canonical stalled CoreMark at exactly\n  4,296,564 bracketed cycles. It measures median Gowin 96.490 MHz\n  versus a reproduced champion 95.961 MHz, only 0.55 percent higher\n  and below acceptance. The final proposal also removes the redundant\n  EX payload-valid mask in this same capture-qualification optimization.\n  Probes of registered load formats, fused RF selection and registered\n  RF read controls regressed and are excluded from the final design.\nhypothesis: |\n  Apply validity and handshake authorization once at each state\n  acceptance boundary instead of also using them as serial data muxes.\n  This is one local control-factoring micro_opt. Preserve pipeline\n  topology, all instruction latencies, the current RF, load formatter,\n  ALU, multiplier/divider, fetch queue, predictor and nret=1.\n\n  In EX construct every payload field unconditionally from the complete\n  registered instruction and operands. Assign payload.valid = in.valid\n  explicitly and preserve all original target/trap/result calculations.\n  Remove the outer if(in.valid) zeroing of the entire payload. Keep the\n  existing mutually exclusive held/completed/fast masked-OR reg_d and\n  all current emission conditions. fast_emit already requires in.valid\n  and actual instruction advance; therefore every non-emitting EX/MEM\n  bubble still becomes exactly zero. A pending payload is captured only\n  on a genuine valid blocking launch, so unconditional construction\n  does not expose invalid work to completion. Do not change capture\n  priorities, pending metadata, writer suppression or recovery rules.\n\n  Use instruction ownership rather than transfer events in the operand\n  DATA selection masks. Fast ownership requires valid nonblocking EX\n  work and no pending instruction. Link ownership additionally chooses\n  the direct-jump link. Completed-source ownership is pending_q with\n  its captured, trap-qualified payload. MEM ownership is its current\n  valid, trap-qualified EX/MEM producer. Remove fast_emit/link_emit/\n  completed_emit and wb_accept from forwarding data masks while\n  retaining operation-kind, reg_write, nonload, source provenance, x0,\n  target alignment and final trap qualification. Owner kinds remain\n  mutually exclusive. Keep independent older matches and youngest\n  qualified-writer priority so a suppressed trapping writer exposes\n  the correct older source. Loads never forward effective addresses.\n\n  Keep all transfer events unchanged for unit request/consume, EX/MEM\n  movement, MEM acceptance, predictor training, retirement and physical\n  register writes. The same hazard hold/flush controls continue to\n  govern complete operand capture. During an older dmem wait or an\n  unfinished M result data candidates may be transient, but capture\n  is inhibited. A pending result is accepted only when execute_busy\n  releases it; reset and accepted recovery clear the operand bank.\n  Prove equivalence at the acceptance boundary, not for unobserved\n  combinational data during a hold. Never accept an unavailable youngest\n  load or M result by falling back to an older RF or MEM value.\n\n  For replacing decoded provenance, compare incoming sources directly\n  against the current decoded writer that will enter EX, before the\n  late hold-dependent next-tag mux. Compare concrete fast and pending\n  MEM destinations independently with the incoming source. Capture\n  these matches only through the existing decoded acceptance. When\n  replacement is possible MEM is not held and pending work is complete;\n  a held MEM candidate cannot coincide with new decode capture. Preserve\n  all original provenance rebasing during actual holds. Keep effective\n  next-tag diagnostics used by tests without putting their late mux\n  back into the matching data path. Retain final result/trap qualification\n  after matching exactly as the original forwarding policy requires.\n\n  Preserve every top-level port, full PC/address, default-illegal and\n  SYSTEM policy, alignment trap, real and ALTOPS M result, exact RVFI\n  operands/successors/memory fields, contiguous retirement order and\n  exactly-once memory effects. Extend directed tests for idle/invalid\n  EX records, launch bubbles, held requests, stale pending ownership,\n  same-rd producer ages, trap-suppressed fallback, WB draining during\n  holds, dependent loads, blocking completion, reset and recovery.\n  Existing zero-bubble and immutable-operand assertions remain intact.\n  Compare accepted operand values with independent architectural\n  results; preserve all existing unit, formal, stalled ISS and canonical\n  CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB/marker gates.\n\n  Estimate six percent higher fitness with unchanged cycles and low\n  confidence pending complete candidate vendor timing. The component\n  measurements do not establish an accepted improvement. At unchanged\n  cycles acceptance requires median Fmax above 100.375206 MHz and\n  fitness above 233.61364. Removing redundant control masks can shorten\n  both fast-result capture and operand delivery without extra flops;\n  the competing ALU/load-return paths and vendor mapping may cap gain.\n  Judge all three placement options and actual bracketed throughput.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Construct payload unconditionally with explicit in.valid and\n      preserve existing emission masks, zero bubbles and launch capture.\n      Expose mutually exclusive fast/link/pending ownership without\n      readiness/consume gates, retaining writer/trap qualification and\n      all unit, hold, pending, recovery and training behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Feed owner-qualified concrete producers to operand selection;\n      retain actual transfer events and capture interlocks. Compare\n      incoming MEM sources with concrete fast and pending destinations\n      before late transfer controls; retain effective-tag diagnostics.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      On decoded replacement match the concrete current decoded writer\n      that will enter EX rather than a hold-selected next tag. Preserve\n      all registered provenance association, hold rebasing, reset/squash\n      priorities and complete operand capture.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace transfer-qualified data masks with instruction-owner\n      qualification while preserving registered matches, youngest-writer\n      priority, independent older fallback, final traps, x0 and PC/imm.\n      Keep output semantics exact whenever operand capture is authorized.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every zero-bubble, result, trap and immutable-payload check.\n      Add invalid-record, owner exclusivity, held launch/completion,\n      consumed stale result, reset and squash cases. Verify pending\n      capture still requires a valid authorized instruction.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check accepted operand equivalence under holds, unavailable loads\n      and M results, same-rd producer ages and trap fallback. Exercise\n      producer drain, consecutive completions, simultaneous recovery,\n      bus stalls and reset. Preserve exact RVFI, order, request stability,\n      zero bubbles and exactly-once memory effects.\nYAML\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np='cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml'\nh=yaml.safe_load(open(p));jsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Schema valid:',h['id'],h['category'])\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import Counter\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe/r15_control/formal/cores/bench/checks')\nprint('Control-only formal status:',Counter(x.read_text().strip() for x in p.glob('*/status')))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
