{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"The smaller prototype is the strongest tested variant: 97.913 MHz median Fmax, about 2.03% above the champion, with unchanged CoreMark cycles and passing pipeline and ISS checks. That remains below acceptance. I’ll record those limits and one final unmeasured refinement that combines fast-result, jump-link, and emission selection at EX/MEM capture."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['motivation'] += '\\\\nThe prototype with both ownership qualification and unconditional EX\\\\npayload construction measures 90.029/97.913/97.913 MHz, median\\\\n97.913 MHz: 2.03 percent above the champion and still below acceptance.\\\\nIt uses 6037 LUT4 and 2689 FF versus 6204/2689, passes all 51 pipeline\\\\ncases and the unchanged direct-EX suite, eight instruction ISS cosims\\\\nand canonical stalled CoreMark at 4,296,564 cycles. The control-only\\\\ncomponent also passes all 53 unchanged fast formal checks in a private\\\\ncopy of the framework; the final combined design still needs formal.\\\\nThe proposal below adds an unmeasured capture-selection refinement;\\\\nthese prototype results are evidence about its components, not a win.\\\\n'\nanchor='  '\nneedle='Use instruction ownership rather than transfer events in the operand'\ninsert='''For the final EX/MEM alu_result input, combine result-kind and fast\nemission controls before masking words. Override only reg_d.alu_result\nwith four parallel terms: held reg_q.alu_result under held_emit,\ncompleted_payload.alu_result under completed_emit, the native binary-\ndecoded alu_result under fast_emit && \"'!in.ctrl.is_jump, and PC+4\nunder fast_emit && in.ctrl.is_jump. This removes the separate wide\njump-link data mux before the emission mask. Keep every other field'\"'s\nexisting masked-OR update and preserve completely zero bubbles.\nRetain payload's original jump-link choice for valid blocking JALR\nlaunch into pending_payload_q, including alignment/trap and prediction\nmetadata. Keep existing fast arithmetic and link forwarding sources\nseparate. Do not add one-hot ALU opcode flops or change ADD/SUB,\nbarrel shifters, comparators or M arithmetic. This final refinement is\nnot present in the measured 97.913 MHz prototype and has not been timed.\n\n'''\nassert needle in h['hypothesis']\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'].replace(needle,insert+needle)\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'].replace('The component\\\\nmeasurements do not establish an accepted improvement.','The measured 2.03 percent prototype gain is below acceptance; the\\\\nsix percent estimate is for the final emission/link fusion, not that\\\\nmeasured prototype. No accepted improvement has been established.')\nh['changes'][0]['description']+='\\\\nFuse native fast-ALU versus PC+4 choice and fast emission in the\\\\nEX/MEM result bank, alongside held/completed sources. Preserve\\\\noriginal link capture in the pending JALR launch payload; retain\\\\nbinary ALU selection and all native arithmetic implementations.\\\\n'\nh['changes'][4]['description']+='\\\\nCheck direct-jump fast link selection separately from JALR launch\\\\nand completion links, including non-emission and misaligned traps.\\\\n'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=76))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261002-001-r15s0' and h['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert all(x['file'].startswith(('rtl/','test/test_')) for x in h['changes'])\nprint('Validated',p,'with',len(h['changes']),'scoped changes')\nprint('Prototype fitness:',97.913*1e6*10/4296564)\nPY\ngit status --short\nls -l cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r15s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
