ine: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns worst path spanning 156 cells through operand\\nforwarding, the ALU, and execute logic. There are no prior micro_opt\\nattempts or distilled lessons. The ALU contains separate signed and\\nunsigned division and remainder expressions; their deep combinational\\narithmetic is the strongest suspected timing bottleneck. Since every\\ninstruction shares this clock, a faster divider can improve CoreMark\\nthroughput even when CoreMark executes few divisions.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapath with a single shared,\\nfully combinational, explicitly unrolled radix-2 non-restoring unsigned\\nquotient-and-remainder engine. Preserve the existing ALU interface,\\nzero-cycle combinational latency, pipeline registers, bus stalls, and\\nnret=1 retirement contract. Th\n…[12285 of 15357 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a233015e41b37309]…\nll priority\\nfor valid as dictated by the existing hazard controls.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Qualify the load-use source-address comparison by imem_ready now\\nthat fetch exposes raw instruction bits during invalid bus cycles.\\nAvoid redirect-derived instruction masking or IF-valid gating in\\nthe comparison cone. Preserve all dmem, execute-busy, redirect,\\npipeline-hold, and MEM/WB forwarding-retention priorities.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed bubble-isolation regressions using deterministic bus\\nstalls: taken branches/JAL/JALR with wrong-path stores and DIV,\\nimem-not-ready data containing LOAD/STORE/DIV/illegal encodings,\\nload-use release, and a branch held behind an older dmem operation.\\nAssert exact retirement PCs, strict order, captured source values,\\nexpected results and traps, bounded divide completion, and exactly\\nonce memory effects. Retain all existing assertions and gates