{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d['id'], d['category'], d['title'], 'fitness',d['fitness'], 'MHz',d.get('fmax_mhz'), 'cycles',d.get('cycles'))\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261002-001-r4s0':\n  print(json.dumps(d.get('hypothesis'),indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-847e570 micro_opt Baseline retest for cores/bench fitness 12.12 MHz 5.442 cycles 4491485\nhyp-20261002-001-r1s0 micro_opt Share a combinational non-restoring divider across DIV and REM fitness 14.25 MHz 6.402 cycles 4491485\nhyp-20261002-002-r1s1 structural Isolate division in a bounded multicycle execution unit fitness 98.49 MHz 44.239 cycles 4491817\nhyp-20261002-003-r1s2 predictor Small tagged bimodal predictor removes correctly predicted redirect bubbles fitness 13.25 MHz 5.577 cycles 4208674\nhyp-20261002-001-r2s0 micro_opt Remove redirect-driven payload masking with validity-only bubbles fitness 98.5 MHz 44.244 cycles 4491817\nhyp-20261002-002-r2s1 structural Register branch recovery at the EX/MEM boundary fitness 89.94 MHz 43.624 cycles 4850577\nhyp-20261002-003-r2s2 predictor Timing-conscious tagged prediction on the multicycle-divider champion fitness 113.27 MHz 47.673 cycles 4208611\nhyp-20261002-001-r3s0 micro_opt Separate the memory address register from the general ALU result fitness 126.93 MHz 53.422 cycles 4208611\nhyp-20261002-002-r3s1 structural Split execute into fast and registered completion paths fitness 131.7 MHz 58.072 cycles 4409538\nhyp-20261002-003-r3s2 predictor Decouple predicted fetch with a compact four-entry flow-through queue fitness 121.1 MHz 48.238 cycles 3983322\nhyp-20261002-001-r4s0 micro_opt Precompute forwarding matches and flatten EX operand selection fitness 133.52 MHz 58.874 cycles 4409538\n{\n  \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 131.70 at median Gowin Fmax 58.0