{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_17", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ('hyp-20261002-001-r2s0','hyp-20261002-001-r3s0'):\n  print(d['id']); print(json.dumps(d.get('hypothesis'), indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-001-r2s0\n{\n  \"motivation\": \"The registered divider champion scores 98.49 at a median 44.239 MHz,\\nwith 4,491,817 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported 29.376 ns,\\n52-cell worst path now crosses ID, EX, IF, hazard logic, and ID again.\\nFetch currently replaces the entire instruction with a NOP on redirect\\nor instruction-bus stall, so late recovery drives instruction bits,\\nregister-file read addresses, decode, and load-use comparisons. ID also\\nclears its entire pipeline payload on a flush. These redundant bubble\\nencodings enlarge the recovery control cone even though validity already\\nsuppresses execution. The prior micro_opt attempt retained a deep\\ncombinational divider and gained only 17.57 percent over baseline; that\\narithmetic bottleneck has already been removed in the current champion.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Represent fetch/decode bubbles solely through the existing valid bit,\\nremoving late redirect and imem-stall signals from instruction payload\\nmasking and from the synchronous clear of ID/EX data. This is one local\\ncontrol-cone optimization, with the same pipeline boundaries, arithmetic\\nunits, branch penalty, memory interface, and nret=1 retirement contract.\\n\\nIn if_stage, always expose raw imem_data as out.instr. Retain the current\\nout.valid qualification and PC update priorities: reset first, accepted\\nEX redirect next, then ordinary advance when not stalled. Decode,\\nimmediate generation, and register-file read addresses must depend on\\nthe raw fetched instruction rather than a redirect-selected NOP.\\n\\nIn id_stage, preserve the full reset initialization, but a nonreset flush\\nmust clear only reg_q.valid. Give the non-valid payload fields a separate\\nupdate condition based only on !stall; they may capture raw data on a\\nflush when not stalled, or retain old data when stalled. Neither flush\\nnor input validity may select zero or disable capture for those fields.\\nUpdate valid with reset/flush priority, otherwise capture in.valid when\\n!stall, otherwise hold. This removes the late f\n…[9602 of 12674 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d98491e795f610c1]…\ne on the output bundle's effective-address field as in\\nthe measured prototype. Preserve reset, data-memory\\nholds, divider payload handling, result forwarding, prediction\\nrecovery and exactly-once instruction advancement. Keep the\\ngeneral ALU and jump/divide result muxes off this address path.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Use the dedicated effective address for dmem_addr, alignment\\nchecking, lane masks, load extraction and aligned RVFI memory\\naddresses. Retain write-data replication, side-effect gating,\\ntrap behavior, and retained WB data during memory stalls.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed checks of forwarded load/store addresses, offsets\\nand carry cases, byte/halfword lanes, misalignment traps and\\nstable exactly-once memory transactions under bus backpressure.\\nExercise nearby ALU, multiply and divide instructions and verify\\nthe existing RVFI operand, memory, PC and order contracts.\\n\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
