file BSRAMs and changes the limiting cone,\nwith area still below the 10,000-LUT target. All five existing register-\nfile tests pass on the probe. Median placement timing and full-pipeline\nvalidation are still being checked; option-0 alone is not a scored\nfitness result. Ignored probe files are under\ncores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe/flop_rf/ and are experimental\nevidence only; the implementation must be rebuilt from this description.\n\nRetain all existing tests and add a register-file scoreboard covering\nall 32 addresses on both ports, concurrent writes/read collisions,\nx0 priority, disabled writes, random data, and reset after writes.\nRequire unchanged pipeline tests, formal, RVFI cosim in zero-wait and\nstalled modes, and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker/OOB gates. Compare\nbracketed cycles to the champion: this semantics-preserving change\nshould keep 4,409,538 cycles. At unchanged cycles, acceptance needs\nmedian Fmax above approximately 66.807 MHz. The estimate is an 8 percent\nfitness gain, with uncertainty from routing the extra flops and the\nnew competing recovery path. Use the evaluator's actual median Gowin\nFmax times bracketed iterations/cycle, without crediting RVFI pruning.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/reg_file.sv','description':'''Replace the dynamically indexed storage/read implementation with\n31 constant-index clocked register words, x0 wiring, per-port\none-hot masked-OR read reductions, and the existing write-first\nbypass priority. Preserve synchronous reset, every bit, ports,\ncombinational reads and synchronous writes. Prevent RAM inference\nthrough the RTL structure, without synthesis-preservation attributes.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_reg_file.py','description':'''Retain every existing assertion and add a deterministic scoreboard\nchecking all register addresses on both read ports, concurrent\nwrites and write-first collisions, same-address dual reads, x0\nwrites/reads, disabled writes, random data, and reset after nonzero\ncontents. Keep pipeline, formal and cosim contracts unchanged.\n'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=76))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated and validated cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r5s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
