{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id')=='hyp-20261002-001-r6s0':\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ('id','title','critical_path','expected_impact')},indent=2))\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id')=='hyp-20261002-001-r6s0':\n  print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ('id','title','critical_path','expected_impact')},indent=2))\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261002-001-r6s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Register complete ALU operand choices ahead of execute\",\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_1_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_31_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -10.829,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 21.123,\n    \"logic_cells\": 42,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 6,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n  }\n}\nMake each EX ALU operand a single masked-OR selection from registered\ndata, with its complete source choice registered at the ID/EX edge.\nThis is one operand-delivery timing optimization: remove late WB data\nselection and serial forwarding-then-PC/immediate selection. Preserve\npipeline depth, arithmetic and instruction acceptance timing.\n\nRegister final WB data before the existing MEM/WB boundary. Add wb_data\nto mem_wb_t; on ordinary MEM capture assign\nin.ctrl.mem_to_reg ? load_data : in.alu_result, using existing aligned\nand sign/zero-extended load_data. WB w_data becomes a direct wire from\nwb_data. Reset clears it; hold_wb retains it while valid clears exactly\nas today. Preserve destination/write metadata and held-WB forwarding\neligibility. Existing alu_result/read_data fields can remain, but must\nnot recreate the late WB mux for any timed consumer.\n\nAlongside existing three-bit raw-register forwarding selections,\nregister independent four-bit one-hot ALU source selections in core.\nBits 0,1,2 choose ID/EX base, next EX/MEM producer and next MEM/WB\nproducer; bit 3 chooses PC for A or immediate for B. Expose just\nnext_alu_a_pc and next_alu_b_imm from id_stage's exact ID/EX next-control\nchoice: reset or flush clears them; otherwise a hold uses current\nregistered is_auipc/alu_src, and an advance uses in.valid-qualified\ndecoded controls. Do not route the entire ID/EX next-state datapath.\n\nOn reset or flush initialize both ALU selectors to 4'b0001. Otherwise\nregister A as {next_alu_a_pc, next_fwd_rs1 & {3{!next_alu_a_pc}}} and B\nas {next_alu_b_imm, next_fwd_rs2 & {3{!next_alu_b_imm}}}. Refresh every\nedge, including holds, exactly as raw forwarding provenance does now.\nMatch actual producers entering or remaining in EX/MEM and MEM/WB;\ndo not substitute current-cycle destination tags.\n\nForm alu_a directly as the OR of four masked values: in.rs1_val,\nfwd_ex_mem, fwd_mem_wb and in.pc. Form alu_b similarly from in.rs2_val,\nfwd_ex_mem, fwd_mem_wb and in.imm. Each mask comes directly from its\nregistered selection bit. Remove the serial is_auipc/alu_src mux after\nraw forwarding. Preserve the separate original raw rs1/rs2 forwarding\nnetwork for branches, JALR, stores, held-operand refresh and RVFI;\nPC/immediate selection must never replace architectural operands.\nMUL/DIV request capture receives the equivalent new ALU operands.\n\nKeep flop-bank storage, decoder legality, real/ALTOPS arithmetic,\npending operations, load-use bubbles, bus backpressure, redirect\ntiming, predictor training, misalignment traps, exact-once side\neffects and nret=1 IO/RVFI unchanged. This adds eight selector flops;\nsynthesis can eliminate redundant WB result flops.\n\nAn isolated early-WB probe reached only 71.104 MHz on placement 1,\nwhile isolated complete ALU provenance reached 67.944 MHz. The combined\nprobe reaches 74.744 MHz on placement 1 versus the champion's 70.604,\nwith 5,398 logic cells, 2,033 registers, 44 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs and\ntwo DSPs. Its worst arrival is 18.674 ns, launching from registered\nwb_data into EX. The unchanged existing pipeline suite passes. These\nare exploratory measurements, not an accepted tournament result.\nRequire all three vendor placements, exact stalled CoreMark CRC/UART\nand markers, unchanged formal checks and full instruction cosims.\nAt unchanged cycles acceptance requires median Fmax above 73.852 MHz.\nRouting of the remaining branch/ALU paths is the principal risk.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
