{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"The final direction is to precompute operand-independent recovery predicates in decode. This keeps the current recovery and predictor-update timing, while removing late legality and alignment gates after branch comparison. The earlier combined attempt paired this change with delayed training; I’m testing the prequalification alone on the current champion."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY' > cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe/branch_control_probes.log 2>&1\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport json\nroot=Path('cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe')\ndef probe(name):\n p=root/name\n r=build('.',p/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',1,p/'timing/gowin_p1')\n (p/'timing_p1.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2))\n print(name,json.dumps(r),flush=True)\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=2) as pool:\n list(pool.map(probe,['prequalified_resolution','shared_native_compare']))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_52", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,jsonschema,yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-001-r7s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261002-001-r7s0\ntitle: \\\"Precompute direct-transfer recovery predicates during decode\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 167.71 iterations/sec at 73.952 MHz with 4,409,538\n  bracketed CoreMark cycles. A fresh unchanged Gowin placement-0 run\n  reproduces its 21.123 ns worst path: ID/EX operands, forwarding, branch\n  comparison, recovery qualification and high-fanout decode clear.\n  Prior micro_opt attempts addressed division, memory addresses, forwarding\n  and register-file delivery. Round 6's combined recovery prequalification\n  and delayed training reached 73.885 MHz on the older operand datapath;\n  delayed training alone regressed. The current champion already improves\n  final WB data and ALU source selection. Isolating static recovery\n  prequalification now targets the remaining EX control cone without\n  introducing the learning delay of those predictor attempts.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move only operand-independent direct-transfer recovery and training\n  qualifications across the existing ID/EX register. Keep the current\n  branch comparator, forwarding, predictor table, immediate EX recovery,\n  training-update timing and all instruction latencies. This is one\n  local control-logic retiming optimization, with no new execution stage\n  or predictor policy.\n\n  Add prediction_wrong_taken, prediction_wrong_not_taken and\n  prediction_train_eligible bits to id_ex_t. In ID default both mismatch\n  bits to the actual fetch snapshot's prediction_selected. Define direct\n  eligibility as decoder-legal branch or direct JAL with word-aligned\n  direct_target; JALR waits for its existing registered actual target.\n  For an eligible branch set wrong_taken to \"'!prediction_selected OR\n  (direct_target != predicted_target), retaining wrong_not_taken as\n  prediction_selected. For eligible direct JAL set both mismatch bits\n  to !prediction_selected OR (direct_target != predicted_target).\n  Ordinary/illegal instructions, JALR and misaligned direct targets\n  retain the defaults. Capture, reset, flush and hold these fields with\n  the existing instruction/prediction bundle. Reuse the existing target\n  adder and prediction snapshot; add no lookup or wide datapath mux.\n\n  In EX, when no blocking payload is pending, select the two saved\n  mismatch bits directly with branch_cond. Both bits agree for\n  nonbranches, so this selection needs no following late opcode,\n  legality or misalignment qualification. Preserve branch_taken and\n  actual trap/RVFI successor calculations. A misaligned taken branch\n  still traps and falls through; an untaken branch with that target\n  remains legal, and stale predictions are corrected in both cases.\n\n  When a blocking payload is pending, default prediction_wrong to its\n  captured pending_prediction_q. Only a captured legal jump replaces it\n  with !pending_prediction_q OR (pending_payload_q.branch_target !=\n  pending_predicted_target_q). Use the authoritative registered JALR sum\n  and captured launch-time trap; MUL/DIV stale predictions still recover\n  only on final advance. Preserve train_valid and redirect'\"'s existing\n  final-advance gates and redirect_target.\n\n  For fast instructions drive train_eligible from the saved direct\n  eligibility bit. For pending completion, eligibility is a captured\n  legal jump with aligned registered branch_target. Preserve train_pc,\n  train_jump, train_taken and train_target and update the BTB on exactly\n  the current edge. Add no training-event register or delayed learning.\n  Eligibility no longer depends on branch_taken through ctrl_with_trap:\n  direct legality and alignment are already known in ID. Preserve\n  tag-qualified stale-entry invalidation and actual fetch snapshots.\n\n  Keep decoder defaults/validation, reset/flush/hold priorities, held\n  operand refresh, registered next-producer forwarding, pending-operation\n  capture/consumption, real and ALTOPS arithmetic, load-use bubbles, both\n  bus handshakes, traps, exactly-once side effects and nret=1 ports intact.\n  The intended gain is less serial control logic after forwarded branch\n  comparison at a cost of three metadata flops and no CoreMark cycles.\n  Competing ALU/memory paths and routing may cap the gain. Estimate eight\n  percent higher fitness with medium confidence; unchanged cycles require\n  median Gowin Fmax above 77.354 MHz to beat the 4.6 percent acceptance\n  margin. This estimate is not an accepted fitness measurement.\n\n  Require unchanged vendor timing, unit, fast formal, stalled RVFI ISS\n  cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/marker gates. Exercise all six\n  branch kinds, both directions and prediction snapshots, wrong direct\n  targets, ordinary/illegal stale entries, misaligned taken versus untaken\n  transfers, changed JALR targets, blocking completions and reset. Cover\n  EX/MEM and retained-WB forwarding, load-use and simultaneous bus stalls.\n  Adapt direct-EX packed stimulus to the new fields and its exact 267-bit\n  ID/EX width assertion, retaining every existing architectural check.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add the two recovery-outcome mismatch bits and direct-transfer\n      eligibility bit to id_ex_t, preserving downstream bundle types.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Compute static mismatch outcomes and direct eligibility from\n      validated decode, existing direct_target and the fetch prediction\n      snapshot; register them with the existing ID/EX priorities.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Select saved mismatch outcomes with branch_cond for fast instructions\n      and captured prediction/target/trap metadata for blocking completion.\n      Use saved direct eligibility for training; preserve update timing,\n      recovery target/latency, architectural traps and side effects.\n      Remove unused recovery locals without changing arithmetic logic.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Extend packed ID/EX layout and exact width check to 267 bits and\n      populate correct recovery metadata in direct EX stimulus. Cover\n      direction/target disagreements, stale predictions, alignment traps\n      and held completion, retaining all existing assertions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Extend exact branch/recovery checks across six comparison kinds,\n      forwarding, load-use, bus holds, stale predictions, misalignment\n      and reset; preserve exact RVFI operands, successors, traps, order\n      and exactly-once side-effect assertions.\n''')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261002-001-r7s0' and d['category']=='micro_opt'\nprint('Revised hypothesis written and schema validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
