{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_41", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261002-002-r6s1','hyp-20261002-002-r8s1','hyp-20261002-002-r9s1']:\n  print(r['id'],r['title']); print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-002-r6s1 Register predictor training at the execute advance boundary\nInsert one registered predictor-training packet between EX resolution\nand the existing tagged predictor's table update. Capture train_valid,\ntrain_pc, train_eligible, train_jump, train_taken and train_target on\nevery edge in core.sv. Feed if_stage training exclusively from this\npacket. Keep the existing combinational EX redirect and redirect_target\nconnection to IF and ID, the prediction lookup, all table dimensions,\ntags, targets and two-bit counter policy unchanged. This is one\nstructural retiming of the predictor-maintenance path, not a change\nto prediction capacity or algorithm and not an extra issue stage.\n\nThe packet valid bit records exactly the existing final EX advance:\nin.valid && !stall && !reset && !execute_busy. It is assigned anew\neach edge, including during memory and blocking-operation holds;\nnever retain a consumed valid packet when the pipeline stalls.\nCapture a completed MUL/DIV/JALR instruction only on its final consume\nedge, with the original pending PC and resolved target. Capture normal\ninstructions too, including ineligible and illegal resolutions, because\nthe predictor uses them to invalidate a matching stale prediction.\nA packet generated before an imem/dmem stall still updates the table\nonce on the next edge. Reset clears packet validity and table validity,\ncancelling any pending update. Preserve program order of consecutive\ntraining packets; there is no queue or update backpressure.\n\nPerfo