{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' tools/eval/gowin.py\nrg -n '\"'^timing:|timing|cosim|test:'\"' Makefile\nrg --files --hidden -g '*timing*' -g '*.rpt' -g '\"'!**/.git/**'\"' -g '\"'!**/worktrees/**'\"' . | head -80\"", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\n\nV2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\nroute and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\nmodel for this part misses whole classes of paths. The vendor flow is also\ndeterministic and insensitive to circuit-neutral netlist changes.\n\nFmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\na full build of the same RTL; results are deterministic for a given input.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport statistics\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import remove_path\n\nGOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\nGOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\nPART = \"GW2AR-LV18QN88C8/I7\"      # Tang Nano 20K\nDEVICE_VERSION = \"C\"\nPLACE_OPTIONS = (0, 1, 2)\nCST = \"fpga/constraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\"\nSDC = \"fpga/constraints/clock.sdc\"\nSTALL_GEN = \"fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\"\nBUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC = 2700\n\n\ndef gowin_env(base: dict | None, workdir: Path) -> dict:\n    env = dict(os.environ if base is None else base)\n    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n    env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = \":\".join(map(str, libs))\n    env[\"QT_QPA_PLATFORM\"] = \"offscreen\"\n    xdg = workdir / \".xdg\"\n    xdg.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    os.chmod(xdg, 0o700)\n    env[\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"] = str(xdg)\n    return env\n\n\ndef rtl_sources(rtl_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:\n    srcs = sorted(rtl_dir.glob(\"*.sv\"))\n    pkg = rtl_dir / \"core_pkg.sv\"\n    return ([pkg] if pkg in srcs else []) + [p for p in srcs if p != pkg]\n\n\ndef project_tcl(worktree: Path, rtl_dir: Path, bench_sv: str, place_option: int) -> str:\n    files = [*rtl_sources(rtl_dir), worktree / STALL_GEN, worktree / bench_sv,\n             worktree / CST, worktree / SDC]\n    return \"\\n\".join([\n        f\"set_device {PART} -device_version {DEVICE_VERSION}\",\n        *(f\"add_file {f}\" for f in fi\n…[8012 of 11084 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:18827ea8469102b2]…\nnt(f\"  full report: {tr}\")\n    if len(res) > 1 and all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res):\n        print(f\"score Fmax (median): {summarize(res)['fmax_mhz']} MHz\")\n    return 0 if all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res) else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n1:.PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n53:CORE_TARGETS := lint test cosim cosim-build formal formal-deep fpga next loop\n79:\t@echo \"  make cosim TARGET=v1    — RVFI cosim against Python ISS\"\n83:\t@echo \"  make timing TARGET=v1   — Gowin Fmax and worst paths (placement option 0)\"\n106:test:\n112:cosim: cosim-build bench/programs/selftest.elf bench/programs/coremark.elf\n113:\tpython3 -m tools.eval.cosim . $(TARGET)\n115:cosim-build: $(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv) test/cosim/main.cpp\n116:\tbash test/cosim/build.sh\n135:# FPGA timing and area come from the vendor flow, Gowin EDA\n137:fpga: cosim-build bench/programs/coremark.elf\n140:timing:\n178:\trm -rf test/cosim/sim_build sim_build out\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ('hyp-20261002-002-r8s1','hyp-20261002-001-r3s0'):\n  print(d['id'])\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('changes:',json.dumps(d.get('changes'),indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ('hyp-20261002-002-r8s1','hyp-20261002-001-r3s0'):\n  print(d['id'])\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('changes:',json.dumps(d.get('changes'),indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-001-r3s0\nIntroduce a dedicated effective-address datapath and EX/MEM address\nregister for loads and stores, retaining every existing pipeline\nboundary and instruction latency. In EX compute a 32-bit modulo sum\nof the fully forwarded rs1 and the registered immediate independently\nof ALU operand selection, the ALU operation mux, jump-link selection,\nand division-result selection. Capture this address in a separate\nEX/MEM field with the same reset and data-memory hold enable as the\ninstruction it accompanies. The existing alu_result stays responsible\nfor arithmetic writeback and nonload forwarding.\n\nDrive the memory address, access-alignment checks, byte-lane masks,\nload extraction and RVFI aligned memory address from this dedicated\nfield. For valid memory instructions the new address must equal the\nold ALU_ADD result exactly, including wraparound and every forwarded\noperand source. When no memory transaction is active, the bus address\nmay expose the registered sum; continue to qualify read and write\nenables by instruction validity, reset and misalignment. Do not put\na general-ALU-result fallback mux on the memory address output.\n\nKeep address capture independent of division completion and of jump\nresult selection. If a division payload or bubble is emitted, the\naddress is irrelevant because its memory enables are zero. During\ndata-bus backpressure, address, data and masks remain stable with the\nheld EX/MEM instruction, and older WB forwarding remains available.\nPreserve the current load-use interlock, predictor, multicycle divider,\ndecoder legality, ALTOPS formulas and nret=1 top-level contract.\n\nThis is one local datapath specialization, with no new execution\nstage, cache or predictor changes. The proposed benefit is a shorter\narithmetic-to-memory cone and less fanout on the general ALU result.\nCoreMark cycles should be unchanged; at that cycle count, acceptance\nrequires median Gowin Fmax above about 49.87 MHz. Estimate an 8 percent\nfitness gain with medium confidence. A different writeback, multiply\n\n…[6474 of 9546 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5fce96cc2a43a1a6]…\nel younger\\npackets on reset/recovery, with no memory packet on slow completion.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Drive dmem address, write data, enables and load extraction from\\nthe registered memory lane. Preserve aligned RVFI memory fields,\\nalignment traps, accepted-load forwarding and retained WB data.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_ex_stage.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Adapt bundle packing without weakening checks. Exercise memory\\nrequest capture, holds and squash beside fast scalar, jump and\\nblocking completion traffic, including all access widths and faults.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Check consecutive loads/stores, forwarded address and store operands,\\nsigned offsets and carry wrap, every byte lane, alignment traps,\\nlong memory waits, load-use, recovery and reset. Assert stable held\\nrequests, exactly-once effects, exact RVFI and contiguous order;\\nretain all existing tests and unchanged external evaluation gates.\\n\"\n  }\n]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"The earlier dedicated-request experiment exposed a producer-control path that later registered stages have changed. The proposed return stage adds a load dependency cycle, so its timing gain has to cover that cost. I’ll probe the request side on the current champion to see whether it still offers useful timing headroom."}}
