{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261002-002-r9s1':\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Restructure the ID/EX boundary as an instruction record with immutable,\nfully resolved raw and ALU operands. Capture all operand words together\nonly when decode actually accepts an instruction. A held instruction\npreserves every operand bit; remove the second held-source forwarding\ninstance and held-operand rebuilding. Keep reset and accepted recovery\nflush dominant over the hold. Do not add pipeline stages, instruction\nbubbles, speculative memory access, or changes to prediction policy.\n\nEstablish the capture invariant explicitly: every nonzero source of an\naccepted instruction equals the youngest preceding legal register\nwriter's final result. A producer in EX bypasses its fast arithmetic,\njump link, or completed blocking result. A load in EX forces the existing\nload-use bubble; a load in MEM bypasses only on bus acceptance. An older\ngenuine MEM wait prevents decode acceptance. A pending blocking EX\ninstruction prevents decode acceptance until completion can advance;\nits completion edge must bypass its exact captured destination/result.\nOtherwise use the accepted MEM final load/ALU value, then the register\nfile's existing write-first value. Preserve youngest-writer priority,\nnonzero destination checks and alignment-trap write suppression. Check\nthe invariant under long stalls and simultaneous writes before removing\nrepair; an unavailable value must prevent acceptance, never be guessed.\n\nUse this acceptance invariant to specialize normal decode forwarding.\nIt needs only the concrete EX fast, EX link, EX completed and accepted\nMEM candidates plus the write-first register-file base. Remove held\nEX/MEM and retained MEM/WB candidates from this capture network. Their\nvalues are either already in an immutable held operand or unavailable\nduring a decode hold; physical WB writes continue to use valid normally.\nFactor genuine memory hold, reset and recovery controls into the operand\nbank's capture enable/clear instead of every 32-bit candidate mask.\nFor candidate selection use source-specific operation/validity and\ncompletion qualification, with fast/link versus pending completion\nmutually exclusive. Pending completion readiness still controls the\nacceptance decision. Never use a stale completion or a load address\nas data. Preserve existing EX/MEM advance and request/consume signals;\nnew decode candidate eligibility is separate from side-effect emission.\n\nBuild ALU-a from resolved rs1 or AUIPC PC and ALU-b from resolved rs2 or\nthe decoded immediate, without a stall-dependent held/new masked OR.\nWrite raw operands, complete ALU operands and instruction metadata on\nthe same accepted edge; retain them together otherwise. Keep genuine\noperand flops and the existing flop-bank register file. EX and blocking\nunit launch consume these immutable words directly. This single change\nremoves held repair and acceptance controls from operand data selection\nwhile retaining ordinary execution and recovery latency.\n\nKeep nret=1 and all ports, full addresses and PC widths, default-illegal\ndecoding, exact RV32M and ALTOPS results, accepted MEM predictor training,\nexactly-once memory effects and contiguous RVFI retirement. RVFI must\nreport the original accepted operand values. Validate unchanged unit,\nformal and instruction cosim gates and canonical stalled CoreMark CRCs,\nUART literal and marker-bracketed cycles. Judge median vendor Fmax times\nactual iterations/cycle; unchanged cycles require more than 87.795 MHz\nfor acceptance. An estimated 92 MHz would improve fitness about 10%.\nCompeting arithmetic and predictor paths may limit the gain.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
