{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r13s1.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261002-002-r13s1\ntitle: \\\"Separate persistent producer values from memory transaction acceptance\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.34 at median 95.961 MHz and 4,296,564 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. Its worst path traverses the general execute result\n  selection into data RAM. A current-parent dedicated LSU request probe\n  removes that endpoint but reaches only 89.542 MHz, exposing both live\n  load-return forwarding and dmemReady-to-operand/provenance control.\n  Registering raw memory returns passes stalled ISS and CoreMark CRCs,\n  but adds 4.94 percent cycles and regresses median Fmax to 82.758 MHz;\n  it still leaves dmemReady driving operand capture. Therefore the next\n  structural target is the coupling of producer values to transaction\n  acceptance, rather than another load-return or arithmetic stage.\n  The earlier r9s1 immutable-operand attempt was limited by bus-to-decode\n  and target-match logic; the current registered decode and fixed fetch\n  head have since isolated that older competing frontend cone.\nhypothesis: |\n  Partition EX into persistent value-producing lanes and a separately\n  controlled memory request lane at the existing EX/MEM boundary.\n  Operand selection uses the instruction owning a producer position;\n  bus readiness and consume events control movement of instruction\n  records, not whether the producer's 32-bit value enters a bypass mux.\n  Keep every stage boundary, normal/load/M latency, frontend policy and\n  in-order retirement width. Do not add a raw-return stage or arithmetic\n  before the complete ID/EX operand flops.\n\n  Form a dedicated LSU address ADD from complete captured operands,\n  with independent request-address storage. Register store replication,\n  lane mask, read/write eligibility and alignment qualification with\n  the request at the same edge. Drive the timed memory interface from\n  these fields, keeping the general scalar operation, jump-link and\n  blocking-completion result selections out of the address path. Use\n  the dedicated address consistently for load extraction and RVFI.\n  Request side effects still depend on actual fast instruction advance;\n  stalls hold the complete packet, and recovery cancels younger packets.\n\n  Separately make fast arithmetic, direct-jump link, pending completion\n  and MEM final-data candidates continuously observable while their\n  owning records occupy the corresponding producer positions. Fast\n  eligibility depends on registered instruction validity, register-write\n  intent, nonload status, nonblocking operation and target legality.\n  Link eligibility additionally selects a direct jump. Pending-result\n  ownership requires the pending-valid bit, original captured destination\n  and trap-qualified write intent; clear ownership on consume/reset/\n  recovery even though its old payload remains stored. These candidate\n  kinds must be mutually exclusive for an EX-position source match.\n  In particular, a blocking MUL/DIV/JALR must never select the ordinary\n  fast ALU output, and a consumed completion must never remain a writer.\n\n  Remove fast_emit, link_emit, completed_emit and wb_accept from the\n  operand data-selection masks. Use registered source provenance plus\n  producer ownership, operation kind, nonzero destination and final\n  trap qualification. Keep youngest-writer priority and independent\n  older matches so a suppressed trapping writer exposes the right older\n  value. MEM can expose its load/ALU value without io_dmemReady in its\n  data mask: a genuine older memory wait already prevents operand\n  capture. A pending M result may change before done, but execute_busy\n  prevents capture until the exact completion is ready. No unavailable\n  load or pending result is ever accepted, and loads never forward\n  effective addresses as register data.\n\n  Retain the current late handshake controls for actual EX/MEM emission,\n  unit request/consume, MEM acceptance, predictor training, retirement\n  and physical writes. They also govern the operand register bank's\n  capture/hold/clear, with reset and accepted recovery dominant. Accepted\n  operands remain immutable during holds. Separate value ownership from\n  those transfer events explicitly in interfaces and comments; do not\n  rename an emit signal while retaining its dmemReady dependence in the\n  data-selection cone. Keep early destination comparison and provenance\n  rebasing associated with actual next producer positions through holds,\n  load-use bubbles and completion. Values from departed producers must\n  remain recoverable through write-first RF reads.\n\n  This is one producer/consumer topology change: autonomous data lanes\n  feed operand capture, while a transaction lane controls side effects\n  and stage movement. It aims to break the repeatedly exposed memory-\n  readiness-to-wide-bypass cone together with the scalar-result-to-memory\n  cone, without paying an extra load-use cycle. The request-only probe\n  is a negative control, not evidence that the combined partition wins.\n  Preserve nret=1, all external ports, full PCs/addresses, default-illegal\n  decode and SYSTEM policy, alignment traps, real and ALTOPS arithmetic,\n  original RVFI operands/PCs, contiguous order and exactly-once effects.\n  Require unchanged formal, stalled ISS and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/\n  OOB/marker checks. At unchanged cycles, acceptance requires median\n  Gowin Fmax above 100.375206 MHz and fitness above 233.61364. Estimate\n  ten percent fitness improvement with low confidence; vendor routing,\n  capture-enable fanout, the RF and load-return path remain risks.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Define the dedicated memory request record and explicit producer\n      ownership/kind metadata if needed. Preserve all architectural and\n      RVFI field widths and the nret=1 retirement contract.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Separate memory request storage from scalar result capture and\n      expose persistent mutually exclusive fast/link/pending producer\n      ownership independent of emit events. Preserve actual request,\n      consume, emission, memory-hold, recovery and training priorities;\n      pending ownership must end on consume/reset/squash.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive requests and address-dependent formatting/RVFI from the\n      dedicated registered LSU packet. Expose the current trap-qualified\n      final MEM candidate independently of bus acceptance without adding\n      a return stage or changing writeback/retirement timing.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Select persistent value candidates using registered provenance,\n      exclusive producer kinds and write/trap qualification. Remove\n      transaction-acceptance controls from every raw/complete operand\n      data mask while retaining age priority, x0 and PC/immediate choices.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Keep operand words immutable and put unavailable-source and genuine\n      memory/blocking holds on bank acceptance. Preserve reset/recovery\n      dominance, independent age matches and provenance rebasing during\n      held decode, with no instruction accepted from an unavailable lane.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire value ownership separately from instruction transfer events,\n      connect the dedicated request lane, and retain the existing hazard\n      and accepted MEM recovery/training controls and all external IO.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Check persistent ownership through stalls and M launch/completion/\n      consume, direct links, alignment faults, squash and reset. Retain\n      all existing payload, zero-bubble and emission assertions; ensure\n      no completed stale payload advertises a writer after consumption.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Assert that every accepted operand equals the youngest legal older\n      writer despite arbitrary ready signals. Cover multiply/divide/JALR\n      consumers, load-use, long data waits, different same-rd producer\n      ages, trapping younger writers, disappearing WB, all memory widths,\n      request stability, recovery and reset. Preserve exact RVFI, order\n      and exactly-once side-effect assertions and unchanged eval gates.\n''')\nprint(p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
