{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r13s1.yaml')\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('title: \\\"Separate persistent producer values from memory transaction acceptance\\\"','title: \\\"Repartition register reads and persistent producer routing before execution\\\"')\ns=s.replace('  head have since isolated that older competing frontend cone.','''  head have since isolated that older competing frontend cone. A probe\n  combining persistent producer values with the dedicated request lane\n  preserves the champion's cycles and passes stalled ISS/CRC checks, but\n  reaches only 94.536 MHz. Its median placement exposes RF lookup into\n  operand capture. Thus the proposed complete repartition moves RF reads\n  into the existing decode edge as well, while keeping arithmetic after\n  complete operand storage; none of these isolated probes claims a win.''')\ns=s.replace('  Partition EX into persistent value-producing lanes and a separately\\\\n  controlled memory request lane at the existing EX/MEM boundary.','''  Repartition the existing decode, operand-read and execute boundaries\n  so decode captures RF base values, operand read selects persistent\n  producer values, and execute owns scalar arithmetic and a separately\n  registered memory request lane. No stage or instruction latency is\n  added. This is one pipeline topology change with three balanced roles,\n  rather than precomputing arithmetic after incoming load data.''')\ns=s.replace('  ID/EX operand flops.\\\\n\\\\n  Form a dedicated LSU', '''  ID/EX operand flops.\n\n  Read the current explicit flop-bank RF from the fixed registered fetch\n  head's source fields and capture both words with the corresponding\n  decoded record. Keep resettable word flops and balanced read trees;\n  avoid inferred RAM that absorbs complete operand registers. Preserve\n  current-WB write-first behavior on this earlier read. During operand\n  selection, repair a snapshot with a qualified current WB write that\n  appeared since the decode edge. Refresh matching snapshots on every\n  held-decode WB write, so a departed writer cannot leave stale data.\n  WB repair is older than EX and accepted MEM, and never overrides an\n  unavailable younger load. Preserve x0 and squash/reset association.\n  RF lookup ends at decode storage; operand read performs forwarding\n  and PC/immediate selection only, without any added adder or shifter.\n\n  Form a dedicated LSU''')\ns=s.replace('  This is one producer/consumer topology change: autonomous data lanes\\\\n  feed operand capture, while a transaction lane controls side effects\\\\n  and stage movement.', '''  This is one producer/consumer pipeline repartition: early RF snapshots\n  and autonomous result lanes feed operand selection, while the request\n  lane controls memory side effects and stage movement.''')\ns=s.replace('      Define the dedicated memory request record and explicit producer\\\\n      ownership/kind metadata if needed.', '      Define the dedicated memory request record, RF snapshot association\\\\n      and explicit producer ownership/kind metadata if needed.')\ns=s.replace('      Keep operand words immutable and put unavailable-source and genuine\\\\n      memory/blocking holds on bank acceptance.', '''      Capture early RF snapshots with decoded metadata, repair from\n      current qualified WB and refresh matching values during holds.\n      Keep complete operands immutable and put unavailable-source and\n      genuine memory/blocking holds on bank acceptance.''')\ns=s.replace('      Wire value ownership separately from instruction transfer events,\\\\n      connect the dedicated request lane,', '''      Drive RF read addresses from the fixed fetch head, route captured\n      and WB-repaired base values to forwarding, wire producer ownership\n      separately from transfer events, connect the dedicated request lane,''')\ns=s.replace('      ages, trapping younger writers, disappearing WB, all memory widths,', '''      ages, trapping younger writers, disappearing WB, early snapshots\n      across decode holds and current-WB repair, all memory widths,''')\np.write_text(s)\nprint('Revised',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
