{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r13s1.yaml')\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('title: \\\"Repartition register reads and persistent producer routing before execution\\\"','title: \\\"Separate producer ownership from pipeline transaction controls\\\"')\nstart=s.index('  head have since isolated')\nend=s.index('\\\\nhypothesis: |',start)\ns=s[:start]+'''  head have since isolated that older competing frontend cone. A probe\n  combining persistent producer values with the dedicated request lane\n  preserves the champion's cycles and passes stalled ISS/CRC checks, but\n  reaches only 94.536 MHz. Early RF snapshots regress to 90.634 MHz and\n  expose dmemReady-to-next-producer-tag matching. The proposed final\n  topology therefore isolates BOTH producer tags and values from late\n  transaction events, while keeping RF and arithmetic stage placement.\n  Those partial probes are negative controls, not a claimed improvement.\n'''+s[end:]\nstart=s.index('  Repartition the existing decode')\nend=s.index('  Operand selection uses',start)\ns=s[:start]+'''  Partition the operand/execute boundary into an independently generated\n  producer-ownership plane, continuously available result lanes, and a\n  transaction plane that alone controls instruction movement. Add a\n  dedicated registered LSU request lane at the existing EX/MEM edge.\n'''+s[end:]\nstart=s.index('  Read the current explicit flop-bank RF')\nend=s.index('  Form a dedicated LSU',start)\ns=s[:start]+s[end:]\nneedle='  Retain the current late handshake controls for actual EX/MEM emission,'\ninsert='''  Remove transaction controls from NEW provenance formation as well.\n  A decoded record is replaced only when stall_id is false, which\n  implies hold_ex is false; reset/recovery clears it with higher priority.\n  Therefore its next-EX writer tag is simply the current decoded\n  record's destination and possible-write intent, without the current\n  hold_ex destination mux or reset/flush qualification before matching.\n  On a held decoded record, use the existing explicit provenance-rebase\n  updates instead of capturing an incoming tag. Assert this phase\n  condition so a future interlock change cannot silently invalidate it.\n\n  On the same new-record capture edge, genuine MEM hold is false and\n  blocking EX is either absent or completing. Match incoming source\n  addresses against a continuous fast possible-writer tag (include\n  loads, exclude MUL/DIV/JALR) and the owned pending-completion tag.\n  Compare both concrete destinations independently. Do not gate these\n  NEW-match candidates by fast_emit, held_emit or pending_consume;\n  capture already enforces the transfer phase, and held_emit cannot\n  contribute on that phase. Loads remain possible writers until MEM\n  returns final data/trap qualification. A pending completion requires\n  pending ownership but does not place done/consume in the comparator\n  cone. Preserve the existing held-record rebase and source-wait rules\n  so only available final values can ever enter complete operands.\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(needle,insert+needle)\ns=s.replace('  This is one producer/consumer pipeline repartition: early RF snapshots\\\\n  and autonomous result lanes feed operand selection, while the request\\\\n  lane controls memory side effects and stage movement.', '''  This is one producer/consumer topology change: independent tags and\n  autonomous result lanes feed operand selection, while transfer controls\n  govern record movement and the request lane governs memory effects.''')\ns=s.replace('  ten percent fitness improvement', '  eight percent fitness improvement')\ns=s.replace('  fitness_delta_pct: 10','  fitness_delta_pct: 8')\ns=s.replace('      Define the dedicated memory request record, RF snapshot association\\\\n      and explicit producer ownership/kind metadata if needed.', '      Define the dedicated memory request record and explicit persistent\\\\n      producer ownership/kind metadata if needed.')\ns=s.replace('''      Capture early RF snapshots with decoded metadata, repair from\n      current qualified WB and refresh matching values during holds.\n      Keep complete operands immutable and put unavailable-source and\n      genuine memory/blocking holds on bank acceptance.''','''      Preserve existing RF placement and immutable complete operands.\n      Distinguish new-record tag capture from held-record rebasing and\n      assert the capture phase that makes transfer-independent matches\n      valid. Keep memory/blocking readiness on bank acceptance.''')\ns=s.replace('''      Drive RF read addresses from the fixed fetch head, route captured\n      and WB-repaired base values to forwarding, wire producer ownership\n      separately from transfer events, connect the dedicated request lane,''','''      Form new-record producer matches from phase-independent decoded\n      and fast/pending ownership tags, removing the hold-selected next\n      EX tag mux and emission-qualified MEM matches. Connect persistent\n      value lanes and the dedicated request lane,''')\ns=s.replace('''      ages, trapping younger writers, disappearing WB, early snapshots\n      across decode holds and current-WB repair, all memory widths,''','''      ages, trapping younger writers, disappearing WB, all memory widths,\n      transfer-independent matches versus held-record provenance rebasing,''')\np.write_text(s)\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(s),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final topology written and schema valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
