{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if any(d['id'].endswith(s) for s in ['r8s1','r9s1']):\n  h=d['hypothesis']; print(d['id'], h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nprint('GIT')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-002-r8s1 Split EX/MEM physically into a scalar execution-result lane and a\ndedicated registered load/store request lane at the existing boundary.\nKeep the current issue and retirement width, instruction latency,\nprediction policy, operand registers and blocking arithmetic units.\nThis is one execution topology change, with no new general stage.\n\nBuild the request lane directly from complete captured operands:\neffective_address = in.alu_a_val + in.alu_b_val for legal memory\ninstructions, modulo 2^32. Give it independent address storage that\nnever selects the general ALU output, a jump link, or MUL/DIV result.\nAt the same EX/MEM edge capture replicated store data, byte-lane mask,\nread/write eligibility and alignment status from that instruction.\nMove memory request formation before this register boundary so MEM\ndrives the external request from registered memory-specific fields.\nUse the dedicated address consistently for load extraction, alignment\nfaults, byte masks and RVFI memory addresses. Keep general alu_result\nresponsible for scalar writeback and scalar bypass; a load's effective\naddress must never become available register data.\n\nCapture a memory packet only on actual fast EX advance. A genuine\nolder memory wait holds every request field stable. Reset, accepted\nrecovery squash, blocking launch/drain and nonmemory advances clear\nrequest validity and enables; no slow completion populates the memory\nlane. The request remains paired with the original EX/MEM retirement\nmetadata. Preserve