{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-002-r15s1.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261002-002-r15s1\ntitle: \\\"Make operand provenance and bypass selection independent of transfer controls\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 223.34 at median Gowin Fmax 95.961 MHz and\n  4,296,564 bracketed CoreMark cycles. It already separates fetch,\n  decoded metadata and complete execution operands, but its producer\n  matching and operand muxes still predict physical movement using\n  late dmemReady, flush, hold and completion-consume controls. Recent\n  r13s2/r14s2 results expose readiness-to-provenance/operand paths.\n  r13s1 combined persistent routing with RF snapshots and an LSU lane,\n  losing 8.77 percent with a competing branch-successor path. This\n  proposal isolates the operand stage's ownership and capture boundary.\n  Local probes reject result banking alone (96.586 MHz, unchanged\n  cycles), registered-only forwarding (92.076 MHz, 4,554,429 cycles),\n  banking with ownership-only data masks (86.746 MHz, unchanged cycles),\n  and banked raw load returns (96.481 MHz, 4,508,917 cycles). These\n  results identify the omitted late provenance controls as a necessary\n  target and argue against introducing additional dependency bubbles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give the existing decoded/operand-read stage a transfer-independent\n  producer-ownership interface. Register source matches against stable\n  instruction owners, and select continuously available producer words\n  by those matches and architectural eligibility. Keep actual readiness,\n  redirects, launch/consume and emission on instruction movement and\n  operand-bank capture. This is one operand-stage topology change with\n  unchanged pipeline depth, instruction latency, register-file storage,\n  execution arithmetic, memory request path and predictor policy.\n\n  Exploit the existing decoded capture invariant: a fetch head replaces\n  decoded_q only when stall_id is false and neither reset nor accepted\n  recovery applies. On every such capture edge, hold_ex and the load-use\n  flush are false, so the next EX owner is the current decoded record.\n  Form next_ex_tag directly from decoded_q's destination, valid and\n  possible-writer intent. Remove its hold_ex/flush/reset destination and\n  writer muxes. Values on noncapture edges are irrelevant and must never\n  be sampled. Preserve possible load writers and nonzero-source matching.\n\n  Likewise match the incoming fetch-head sources to independently\n  observable EX owners before the late fast_emit/completed_emit/held_emit\n  controls. The possible next MEM writer is either a valid nonblocking\n  current EX instruction, including loads, or the valid captured pending\n  completion owner. A genuine older MEM hold prevents decoded capture,\n  so an additional held-EX/MEM destination arm is unnecessary for these\n  incoming matches. Pending validity and operation classification must\n  distinguish the two owners; a stale pending payload cannot match after\n  consume or cancellation. Completion may be matched before done, since\n  execute_busy prevents capture until it can actually transfer. Do not\n  use a post-handshake destination mux for either source comparison.\n\n  Select EX fast arithmetic, direct-jump link and pending completion\n  values by registered source provenance, their stable owning instruction,\n  nonzero destination and final trap qualification. Fast and link owners\n  exclude all blocking MUL/DIV/JALR instructions and a pending completion;\n  completion ownership requires pending_valid and its original captured\n  write intent. Remove dmemReady, fast_emit, link_emit, pending_consume\n  and wb_accept from the wide data-source masks. The MEM candidate may\n  expose its final qualified load/ALU value continuously while its record\n  owns that position: a genuine memory wait prevents operand capture.\n  Retain independent older matches and youngest qualified writer priority,\n  so a trapping younger writer exposes the correct older value. A load\n  in EX remains unavailable and never forwards its effective address.\n\n  Keep actual transfer signals for physical stage updates, incoming\n  instruction acceptance, unit request/consume, memory side effects,\n  training and retirement. Preserve the existing provenance rebasing\n  while decoded_q is held, based on actual movement of older records;\n  departed writers remain recoverable through the write-first RF.\n  Keep complete raw and ALU operand flops immutable during holds, with\n  reset/recovery dominant. No unavailable load or pending result can be\n  accepted merely because a data candidate is visible. Capture must\n  remain blocked until the youngest required value is ready. Add checks\n  that decoded acceptance implies the assumptions used to simplify tag\n  prediction and that every accepted nonzero operand equals the youngest\n  preceding qualified writer's exact value.\n\n  This removes handshake-dependent destination prediction as well as\n  handshake-dependent word selection, addressing the path left behind\n  by the ownership-only probe. Do not add operation-result banks, LSU\n  lanes, raw-return stages, RF snapshots, synchronous RF RAMs, arithmetic\n  before complete operands, or extra result-dependency bubbles.\n  Preserve nret=1 and all top-level ports, full PCs and addresses,\n  default-illegal and SYSTEM decoding, alignment traps, real and ALTOPS\n  RV32M results, exact RVFI operands/successors, contiguous order and\n  exactly-once memory effects. Require existing unit tests, unchanged\n  formal, stalled ISS cosim and canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/OOB/marker\n  validation. Score median vendor Fmax times measured bracketed cycles.\n  At unchanged cycles, acceptance needs Fmax above 100.375206 MHz and\n  fitness above 233.61364. Project a six percent gain with low confidence;\n  capture-enable/provenance-rebase fanout, RF reads and the unchanged\n  ALU-to-memory path can limit it. Component results are not evidence\n  that the final ownership-and-provenance change crosses acceptance.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Form incoming EX and MEM provenance from stable decoded/current-EX/\n      pending owners, removing late hold/flush/emission destination muxes\n      on edges where decoded capture is enabled. Wire independent bypass\n      ownership qualifiers while preserving all existing transfer,\n      source-wait, hazard, memory, predictor and RVFI controls.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Expose mutually exclusive nonblocking fast/link and valid pending\n      producer ownership, including a possible-writer qualifier for loads\n      used only in matching. Keep real request/consume/emission and recovery\n      timing unchanged. Qualify stale payloads by pending validity and\n      preserve alignment-trap suppression and captured completion data.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Select concrete values using registered provenance and stable\n      ownership instead of transfer enables. Preserve independent older\n      matches, youngest qualified priority, x0, exact raw operands and\n      parallel complete PC/immediate ALU operand selection. Readiness\n      remains on capture interlocks, never on wide data-source masks.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Make the decoded capture invariant explicit and retain actual-transfer\n      provenance rebasing during holds. Keep reset/squash priority and\n      complete operand storage, with no live bypass or held operand repair.\n      Check that simplified owner matches are sampled only on valid\n      replacement edges and remain associated with the same instruction.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every existing exact correctness and latency assertion. Add\n      owner-match checks on decoded acceptance, load/unready completion\n      interlocks, fast/link/completion exclusion, same-rd competing ages,\n      trapping writer fallback, WB drain during holds, long randomized\n      memory stalls, reset and recovery. Check exact captured operands,\n      request stability, retirement order and exactly-once side effects.\n  - file: test/test_ex_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Retain exact results and acceptance checks; exercise independent\n      ownership before completion, across holds, at consumption and after\n      cancellation. Verify that pending data cannot remain an owner after\n      consume/reset/recovery and blocking instructions cannot own fast data.\n''')\nprint('Refined hypothesis written')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
