{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The detailed report confirms a multiplier path, but a JALR recovery path is almost as slow. Both start at the inferred block-RAM register file, so registering multiplication alone may leave Fmax near its current limit. I’ll test a banked flip-flop register file that could shorten both paths without adding instruction cycles."}}
