{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\"|hyp-20261002-002-r7s1|hyp-20261002-002-r3s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261002-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Isolate division in a bounded multicycle execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz and its reported worst path traverses\\nforwarding and the execute ALU across 156 cells. The ALU currently infers\\ncombinational signed and unsigned division and remainder networks, placing\\ndeep arithmetic behind the ordinary EX operand muxes and ahead of the\\nregistered result used for memory addresses and subsequent forwarding.\\nRemoving these networks from single-cycle execution offers much more\\ntiming headroom than a small improvement in instruction throughput. There\\nare no prior structural attempts or recorded lessons in this fixture.\\nSource inspection finds the visible divisions in CoreMark list sizing and\\ninitialization, before the measured iteration loop; its timed list,\\nmatrix, state, and CRC kernels therefore appear unlikely to pay a large\\ndynamic divide penalty. Confirm this with the unchanged bracketed cosim.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches only 5.442 MHz and its reported worst path traverses\\nforwarding and the execute ALU across 156 cells. The ALU currently infers\\ncombinational signed and unsigned division and remainder networks, placing\\ndeep arithmetic behind the ordinary EX operand muxes and ahead of the\\nregistered result used for memory addresses and subsequent forwarding.\\nRemoving these networks from single-cycle execution offers much more\\ntiming headroom than a small improvement in instruction throughput. There\\nare no prior structural attempts or recorded lessons in this fixture.\\nSource inspection finds the visible divisions in CoreMark list sizing and\\ninitialization, before the measured iteration loop; its timed list,\\nmatrix, state, and CRC kernels therefore appear unlikely to pay a large\\ndynamic divide penalty. Confirm this with the unchanged bracketed cosim.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU with one shared, bounded multicycle\\nradix-2 restoring divider, \n…[77499 of 80571 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:872ed9bfc6ead18b]…\nvement\", \"fitness\": 187.23, \"delta_pct\": 11.64, \"vs_baseline\": 1444.8, \"fmax_mhz\": 83.934, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4483027, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5976, \"ff\": 2216, \"seeds\": [73.697, 83.934, 83.934], \"perturbations\": [[0, 73.697, 10], [1, 83.934, 10], [2, 83.934, 10]], \"lutram\": 44, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_3_dmem_3_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -8.569, \"arrival_ns\": 18.864, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T08:30:19.503666Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-02 hyp-20261002-002-r7s1 (improvement, +11.64%): Registering complete ID/EX operands and EX/MEM recovery together isolates EX from incoming bypass selection and outgoing frontend feedback, while prediction limits the extra recovery bubble to misses so Fmax gains outweigh CoreMark's cycle penalty.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
