{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build_all,summarize\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe/predictor')\nr=build_all(Path.cwd(),p/'split64','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',p/'split_timing')\n(p/'split_timing.json').write_text(json.dumps({'results':r,'summary':summarize(r)},indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps(summarize(r)))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"placement_failed\": false, \"fmax_mhz\": 84.312, \"seeds\": [83.934, 84.312, 84.312], \"perturbations\": [[0, 83.934, 10], [1, 84.312, 9], [2, 84.312, 9]], \"lut4\": 6162, \"ff\": 2333, \"lutram\": 22, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"logic_levels\": 10, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_a_val_29_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.914, \"arrival_ns\": 17.208, \"logic_cells\": 10, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_mem\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_34", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r10s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r10s2',\n'title':'Instruction-derived direct targets with separate direction and indirect prediction',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The 32-entry tagged BTB couples conditional direction learning to target\nreplacement and gives direct JALs compulsory/conflict misses even though\nall direct targets are encoded in the current instruction. A canonical\nCoreMark retirement-trace model counts 73,619 successor misses: 55,992\nconditional, 15,638 JAL and 1,989 JALR. Folding the existing 32 entries\nincreases misses, so simply hashing the current BTB is not the proposal.\nDecoupling direction from target storage can remove JAL target misses,\nretain direction state across target conflicts and shrink the wide\nlookup/tag/comparison cone before ID. Recent fetch queues already tested\nstall lookahead; their cycle savings did not survive vendor timing.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the mixed 32-entry BTB with one instruction-qualified predictor:\nexact instruction-derived targets for conditional branches and JAL, a\n64-entry direction-only bimodal table, and a 16-entry fully tagged target\ntable exclusively for JALR. Keep the direct combinational fetch/ID path,\nall pipeline stages, complete operand capture and registered MEM recovery.\nThis is one predictor architecture, with no fetch queue or arithmetic change.\n\nPredecode only validated branch funct3 values, JAL, and JALR funct3=0.\nConstruct the exact sign-extended B/J immediate from the fetched word and\nadd it to its full PC. A legal aligned direct JAL always selects that\nexact target. A conditional branch uses the direction table at index\nPC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8]; on an invalid direction entry use the instruction's\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken sign as the cold prediction. Select no\nmisaligned direct target and make ordinary/illegal encodings fall through.\nThe predecoder is solely a prediction qualifier: retain the authoritative\ndefault-illegal architectural decoder and every existing trap check.\n\nThe untagged direction table holds two-bit saturating counters and reset\nvalid bits. Train only legal aligned conditional branches on the existing\nonce-per-MEM-acceptance event. Allocate 10 for taken or 01 for not taken;\nsubsequent updates saturate using the current table state. JAL, JALR and\nordinary instructions cannot overwrite or invalidate direction counters.\nDirection aliasing affects performance only and never authorizes a side effect.\n\nThe 16-entry JALR table indexes PC[5:2] XOR PC[9:6], retains the complete\n26-bit PC[31:6] tag and aligned full target PC[31:2], and resets validity.\nThe hash plus retained tag uniquely identifies every aligned full PC.\nOnly a validated JALR with a full-tag hit selects its stored target.\nExpose reg_q.ctrl.is_jalr alongside train_jump on the current registered\nMEM training event; only eligible aligned JALR events allocate/update\ntarget entries. Preserve full-tag-qualified invalidation on an accepted\nsame-PC non-JALR or ineligible record, never invalidating an unrelated tag.\nNo live EX result or same-cycle training bypass enters fetch prediction.\n\nCarry the actual chosen prediction through the existing IF/ID and ID/EX\nsnapshot fields, including held and pending instructions. Because direct\nselected targets now come from the identical accepted instruction and PC\nas the architectural direct_target, capture direct_target_match=1 for\nvalidated direct branches/JAL instead of comparing a BTB target against\nanother PC+immediate result. Retain real target comparison and recovery\nfor captured JALR completions; preserve ordinary/illegal stale-prediction\nrecovery as a general invariant. A prediction that is not selected has\nno authority over actual branch outcome, target alignment, link value,\nRVFI successor or architectural trap behavior.\n\nKeep reset/recovery and all PC/ID acceptance priorities unchanged. MEM\ntraining must occur once even on its own redirect edge; held or squashed\nwork cannot train. Preserve nret=1 and every top-level port, full PC and\ntarget widths, load-use and bus semantics, held-operand refresh, contiguous\nRVFI order, exactly-once stores and real/ALTOPS multiply/divide behavior.\nChange no contract or correctness gate. Measure canonical stalled cycles\nand median Gowin Fmax together; extra IF target addition and imem predecode\nfanout are the main physical risks. Trace-model counts are sizing evidence,\nnot measured RTL fitness, and the final implementation must be retested.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the mixed BTB with exact validated direct targets, a 64-entry\nfolded-PC direction table and a 16-entry full-tag JALR-only table.\nImplement cold BTFNT, unchanged saturating direction policy, MEM-event\nupdates and tag-qualified indirect invalidation. Preserve direct fetch,\nfull addresses, acceptance enables and prediction snapshots.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''For validated direct branches/JAL, capture the guaranteed direct-target\nmatch without a wide equality comparator; keep the architectural target\nadder and all captured prediction, operand, hold and flush semantics.\nRetain comparison where an instruction-derived target is not guaranteed.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Expose the resolving registered instruction's is_jalr classification\nas train_indirect alongside the existing accepted-MEM training signals.\nPreserve registered recovery and all existing pending JALR full-target\nvalidation, instruction traps, completion and producer logic.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire the train_indirect event bit from EX/MEM acceptance into IF;\nleave external nret=1 IO and all operand/hazard/recovery wiring intact.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Add cold direct-JAL prediction and link checks, BTFNT warm-up/exit,\nall valid branch funct3 values, reserved encodings, counter saturation,\nfolded-index direction aliases and full-tag indirect collisions. Check\nchanged JALR targets, instruction replacement before acceptance, target\nmisalignment, reset, exactly-once learning through bus/execute holds and\nredirect override. Preserve exact RVFI PCs/operands/traps/order and stores;\nadapt only assertions tied to the documented predictor policy. Require\nunchanged formal, stalled ISS and canonical CoreMark validation gates.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=85))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_34", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r10s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r10s2',\n'title':'Instruction-derived direct targets with separate direction and indirect prediction',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The 32-entry tagged BTB couples conditional direction learning to target\nreplacement and gives direct JALs compulsory/conflict misses even though\nall direct targets are encoded in the current instruction. A canonical\nCoreMark retirement-trace model counts 73,619 successor misses: 55,992\nconditional, 15,638 JAL and 1,989 JALR. Folding the existing 32 entries\nincreases misses, so simply hashing the current BTB is not the proposal.\nDecoupling direction from target storage can remove JAL target misses,\nretain direction state across target conflicts and shrink the wide\nlookup/tag/comparison cone before ID. Recent fetch queues already tested\nstall lookahead; their cycle savings did not survive vendor timing.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the mixed 32-entry BTB with one instruction-qualified predictor:\nexact instruction-derived targets for conditional branches and JAL, a\n64-entry direction-only bimodal table, and a 16-entry fully tagged target\ntable exclusively for JALR. Keep the direct combinational fetch/ID path,\nall pipeline stages, complete operand capture and registered MEM recovery.\nThis is one predictor architecture, with no fetch queue or arithmetic change.\n\nPredecode only validated branch funct3 values, JAL, and JALR funct3=0.\nConstruct the exact sign-extended B/J immediate from the fetched word and\nadd it to its full PC. A legal aligned direct JAL always selects that\nexact target. A conditional branch uses the direction table at index\nPC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8]; on an invalid direction entry use the instruction's\nbackward-taken/forward-not-taken sign as the cold prediction. Select no\nmisaligned direct target and make ordinary/illegal encodings fall through.\nThe predecoder is solely a prediction qualifier: retain the authoritative\ndefault-illegal architectural decoder and every existing trap check.\n\nThe untagged direction table holds two-bit saturating counters and reset\nvalid bits. Train only legal aligned conditional branches on the existing\nonce-per-MEM-acceptance event. Allocate 10 for taken or 01 for not taken;\nsubsequent updates saturate using the current table state. JAL, JALR and\nordinary instructions cannot overwrite or invalidate direction counters.\nDirection aliasing affects performance only and never authorizes a side effect.\n\nThe 16-entry JALR table indexes PC[5:2] XOR PC[9:6], retains the complete\n26-bit PC[31:6] tag and aligned full target PC[31:2], and resets validity.\nThe hash plus retained tag uniquely identifies every aligned full PC.\nOnly a validated JALR with a full-tag hit selects its stored target.\nExpose reg_q.ctrl.is_jalr alongside train_jump on the current registered\nMEM training event; only eligible aligned JALR events allocate/update\ntarget entries. Preserve full-tag-qualified invalidation on an accepted\nsame-PC non-JALR or ineligible record, never invalidating an unrelated tag.\nNo live EX result or same-cycle training bypass enters fetch prediction.\n\nCarry the actual chosen prediction through the existing IF/ID and ID/EX\nsnapshot fields, including held and pending instructions. Because direct\nselected targets now come from the identical accepted instruction and PC\nas the architectural direct_target, capture direct_target_match=1 for\nvalidated direct branches/JAL instead of comparing a BTB target against\nanother PC+immediate result. Retain real target comparison and recovery\nfor captured JALR completions; preserve ordinary/illegal stale-prediction\nrecovery as a general invariant. A prediction that is not selected has\nno authority over actual branch outcome, target alignment, link value,\nRVFI successor or architectural trap behavior.\n\nKeep reset/recovery and all PC/ID acceptance priorities unchanged. MEM\ntraining must occur once even on its own redirect edge; held or squashed\nwork cannot train. Preserve nret=1 and every top-level port, full PC and\ntarget widths, load-use and bus semantics, held-operand refresh, contiguous\nRVFI order, exactly-once stores and real/ALTOPS multiply/divide behavior.\nChange no contract or correctness gate. Measure canonical stalled cycles\nand median Gowin Fmax together; extra IF target addition and imem predecode\nfanout are the main physical risks. Trace-model counts are sizing evidence,\nnot measured RTL fitness, and the final implementation must be retested.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the mixed BTB with exact validated direct targets, a 64-entry\nfolded-PC direction table and a 16-entry full-tag JALR-only table.\nImplement cold BTFNT, unchanged saturating direction policy, MEM-event\nupdates and tag-qualified indirect invalidation. Preserve direct fetch,\nfull addresses, acceptance enables and prediction snapshots.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''For validated direct branches/JAL, capture the guaranteed direct-target\nmatch without a wide equality comparator; keep the architectural target\nadder and all captured prediction, operand, hold and flush semantics.\nRetain comparison where an instruction-derived target is not guaranteed.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Expose the resolving registered instruction's is_jalr classification\nas train_indirect alongside the existing accepted-MEM training signals.\nPreserve registered recovery and all existing pending JALR full-target\nvalidation, instruction traps, completion and producer logic.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire the train_indirect event bit from EX/MEM acceptance into IF;\nleave external nret=1 IO and all operand/hazard/recovery wiring intact.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Add cold direct-JAL prediction and link checks, BTFNT warm-up/exit,\nall valid branch funct3 values, reserved encodings, counter saturation,\nfolded-index direction aliases and full-tag indirect collisions. Check\nchanged JALR targets, instruction replacement before acceptance, target\nmisalignment, reset, exactly-once learning through bus/execute holds and\nredirect override. Preserve exact RVFI PCs/operands/traps/order and stores;\nadapt only assertions tied to the documented predictor policy. Require\nunchanged formal, stalled ISS and canonical CoreMark validation gates.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=85))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Refined hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Refined hypothesis written and schema-valid\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
