{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r10s2.yaml')\nd={'id':'hyp-20261002-003-r10s2','title':'Four-entry predicted fetch stream with empty-queue direct delivery','category':'predictor','motivation':'''The registered-head two-entry predictor queue reached a 4.51 percent gain,\njust below the 4.6 percent acceptance margin. The three-entry version reduced\nCoreMark cycles by 5.13 percent but reached only 81.598 MHz. Registered-only\ndelivery pays an extra refill cycle whenever recovery empties the queue.\nA two-entry flow-through prototype reduces canonical bracketed cycles from\n4,483,027 to 4,196,879, but its 79.954 MHz median still yields only about\n190.51 iterations/sec. The single angle is deeper predicted lookahead with\nempty-queue direct delivery, preserving that avoided refill delay while\ncovering longer backend and instruction-bus stall bursts.\n''','hypothesis':'''Add a four-entry flow-through predicted-fetch queue inside if_stage.\nPreserve the current 32-entry full-tag BTB policy, full target widths,\ncounter updates and exactly-once accepted-MEM training latency. Fetch and\nretain complete predicted instruction snapshots during backend holds;\nconsume saved words during instruction-bus stalls. Use four separate\nconstant-index whole-word flop banks with entry zero always the oldest.\nStore full PC, instruction, prediction_selected, full predicted_target,\nvalid payload and one frontier marker. Never reconstruct queued PCs.\nUse prefix occupancy v0,v1,v2,v3 and fixed shift/append bank enables.\n\nAn occupied queue presents slot zero. An empty queue presents the current\nlive bus word and its current BTB prediction directly, using only v0 for\npayload selection. Qualify validity independently of payload bits. An\nempty live word is consumed immediately if the instruction bus accepts it\nand the backend can accept; do not write it into storage in that case.\nIf the backend holds, save the same accepted live snapshot into slot zero.\nThis eliminates registered-refill bubbles after recovery and ordinary\nqueue drain, while retaining instruction-bus acceptance during backend\nholds. Decode operands only when ID accepts the selected word.\n\nUse these controls from OLD state, all inhibited on reset/recovery:\n  push = imemReady && \"'!v3 && !frontier_wait;\n  pop = v0 && backend_ready;\n  bypass = !v0 && backend_ready && push;\n  stored_push = push && !bypass.\nPush depends on free capacity at cycle start, never on pop. An initially\nfull queue refuses simultaneous replacement; this keeps fetch advancement\nindependent of late hazard/execute readiness. Advance fetch PC once per\npush, including bypass. Store the exact prediction observed at that edge.\nDerive constant-bank append enables without a count or pointer subtract:\n  append0 = stored_push && (!v0 || (pop && !v1));\n  append1 = stored_push && ((v0 && !v1 && !pop) || (v1 && !v2 && pop));\n  append2 = stored_push && ((v1 && !v2 && !pop) || (v2 && !v3 && pop));\n  append3 = stored_push && v2 && !pop.\nAppend wins over shift. Otherwise pop shifts slot1 into slot0, slot2 into\nslot1 and slot3 into slot2. Unwritten/invalid payloads need no reset.\nUpdate prefix occupancy with OLD values:\n  v0_next = stored_push || (v0 && !pop) || v1;\n  v1_next = (v1 && !pop) || v2 || (stored_push && v0 && (!pop || v1));\n  v2_next = (v2 && !pop) || v3 || (stored_push && v1 && (!pop || v2));\n  v3_next = (v3 && !pop) || (stored_push && v2 && !pop).\nThe only valid occupancy patterns are empty, one, two, three and four.\nUse packed vector wires between separately generated flop banks so the\nformal frontend accepts whole-word storage and synthesis avoids indexed\npayload reads. A balanced two-source mask/OR can implement head/live\nselection, but never qualify raw instruction/source-address bits with\nredirect, bus readiness or backend readiness.\n\nHandle raw imemReady locally in IF. Backend holds come only from the\npresented instruction'\"'s load-use dependency, genuine older dmem hold and\nexecute_busy. An available queued head must remain consumable when the\nphysical bus stalls; an unavailable head inserts the existing ID bubble.\nKeep all existing ID flush/hold and held-operand-refresh rules. Accepted\nMEM recovery overrides frontend/backend holds, cancels push/pop/bypass,\nclears occupancy and installs the full resolved target. Correct predictions\nretain queued work. Learn on the existing resolving MEM event, including\nits own redirect edge; queue activity and squashed instructions never train.\n\nBound speculative lookahead at the instruction-memory frontier. If an\naccepted snapshot's predicted successor is outside [0,0x00100000), mark\nthat exact dynamic snapshot, save its full successor and hold the physical\nfetch PC at its accepted address. Accept no duplicate words while waiting;\nthe queued backend drains normally. Carry the marker through ID/EX and\nEX/MEM, including all pending blocking payloads. Only that exact marked\ninstruction's accepted-MEM event authorizes release of the saved full\nsuccessor as actual architectural demand if no recovery is required.\nRecovery/reset cancel the wait; recovery has priority over release. Never\nrelease by PC equality, clamp an architectural demand, truncate addresses\nor suppress symbolic progress. Only one frontier marker may be outstanding.\n\nPreserve nret=1, external IO, full PCs/targets, default-illegal validated\ndecoding, every trap, actual RVFI operands/successors, contiguous retirement\norder, complete operand capture, load-use and memory handshakes, exactly-once\nstores and real/ALTOPS arithmetic. The added frontier bit changes IF/ID to\n99 bits, ID/EX to 329 and EX/MEM to 296; update explicit packed masks and\ndirected-test layouts consistently with numeric/frontend-supported widths.\nDo not modify any evaluation contract. Reimplement from this description:\nprototype artifacts are transient and removed before implementation/eval.\nMeasure canonical bracketed stalled CoreMark cycles and median vendor Fmax\ntogether. Head/live source selection before forwarding is the main timing\nrisk; accepting a depth solely because it saves cycles is insufficient.\n''','expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'medium'},'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Implement four fixed flop snapshots, prefix occupancy, independent\nconservative push, fixed shifts/appends and empty-queue direct delivery.\nPreserve BTB policy and learning latency. Carry exact accepted prediction\nsnapshots and enforce dynamic frontier waiting/release with recovery priority.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'''Make backend/frontend-consumption holds independent of raw imemReady;\nuse presented-head validity for load-use, preserving execute_busy, older\ndmem holds and every existing flush/ID/EX/MEM/WB priority. Let IF handle\nphysical bus acceptance and absence of a consumable instruction.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire backend acceptance readiness and the existing accepted-MEM event's\nfrontier bit into IF. Preserve all complete-operand/producer connections,\nregistered recovery and the entire nret=1 top-level IO contract.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Add one frontier marker to if_id_t, id_ex_t and ex_mem_t, keeping all\nfull PCs, prediction fields and architectural RVFI semantics.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'''Capture, hold and clear the dynamic frontier marker with its accepted\ninstruction and prediction snapshot. Preserve operand capture, target\nmatch and held-operand refresh without further pipeline changes.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Copy the frontier bit into fast and pending payloads and expose it on\nthe existing accepted-MEM training event. Update