{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print(d['id'], d['title'])\n  print('fitness',d.get('fitness'),'fmax',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'),'outcome',d.get('outcome'))\n  h=d['hypothesis']; print(h.get('hypothesis','')[:2000] if isinstance(h,dict) else h[:2000])\n  if d.get('implementation_notes'): print('NOTES',d['implementation_notes'][:2000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-003-r1s2 Small tagged bimodal predictor removes correctly predicted redirect bubbles\nfitness 13.25 fmax 5.577 cycles 4208674 outcome regression\nAdd one 32-entry direct-mapped, fully tagged branch-target buffer with a\ntwo-bit saturating direction counter per entry. Index by fetch PC[6:2],\nstore PC[31:7] as the tag and the full aligned target PC[31:2], and reset\nvalid bits. Read it combinationally from the registered fetch PC; a valid\ntag hit with counter[1]=1 predicts the stored target, otherwise predict\nPC+4. Use this lookup rather than instruction predecode or an IF target\nadder. Train conditional branches on their resolved taken/not-taken\noutcome, allocating at weakly taken (10) or weakly not taken (01), and\ntrain aligned legal JAL/JALR targets as strongly taken (11). Train only\nonce when a valid EX instruction actually advances, never during reset,\nbubbles, or dmem backpressure. Reject misaligned targets.\n\nCarry the predicted successor PC through IF/ID and ID/EX with the\ninstruction. In EX compute the architectural successor using the existing\nforwarded operands, branch/jump resolution, and misalignment handling.\nRedirect and flush only when this actual successor differs from the\ncarried prediction. Check every valid instruction, including ordinary\ninstructions and traps, so a stale BTB hit or