{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_42", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Banked hashed BTB with taken-only allocation preserves useful targets'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 223.34 with 4,296,564 timed CoreMark cycles at\n95.961 MHz. Its 32-entry direct-mapped bimodal predictor produces 73,619\naccepted control-transfer recoveries in the measured interval: 55,992\nconditional branches, 15,638 direct jumps and 1,989 returns. Hot direct\njumps repeatedly miss, showing target conflicts rather than a return-stack\nopportunity. Every legal conditional branch currently allocates a row,\neven on a not-taken miss that needs no target, evicting useful taken paths.\nEarlier attempts mostly changed delivery or maintenance timing, and the\nchampion already has registered fetch and training boundaries. Focus this\nattempt solely on retaining useful predictor entries under conflicts.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the 32-entry tagged bimodal BTB with one conflict-resistant\n128-entry predictor: four indexed 32-entry banks, a reversible XOR index,\nand taken-only allocation on a tag miss. Compute the seven-bit index as\nPC[8:2] XOR PC[15:9], use index[6:5] as the bank and index[4:0] as its row,\nand retain the entire PC[31:9] tag and 30 aligned target bits. This is a\nfull tag: PC[15:9] is contained in the stored tag, so the tag and hashed\nindex uniquely reconstruct PC[31:2]. Do not use partial tags or shorten\ntargets. Mixing address bits disperses hot code with repeated low offsets;\ntaken-only allocation stops irrelevant not-taken misses from replacing\nuseful targets. These are one predictor-conflict policy, with no changes\nto frontend delivery, direction algorithm, recovery timing or execution.\n\nA matching legal conditional branch still updates its existing two-bit\ncounter for either outcome, using the current Boolean saturation equations.\nA conditional miss allocates weakly taken only when actually taken. A\nnot-taken conditional miss leaves the entire addressed row untouched:\nvalidity, tag, target and counter. Legal aligned JAL/JALR allocate or update\nstrongly taken as before. Ineligible events retain exact tag-qualified\nstale-entry invalidation, without erasing another PC's replacement. The\nallocation decision must gate both table writes and the logical post-update\nrow used for forwarding; merely suppressing the write while forwarding an\nimaginary allocation is incorrect.\n\nDeclare each bank's tag, target and counter arrays separately with 32 rows\ninside a constant-index generate block. Read each bank with the five-bit\nrow index, then select the bank with a balanced four-way selection. Keep\nindexed RAM-friendly storage, rather than parallel full-tag comparison\nagainst 128 flop words or a single dynamically indexed 128-row array.\nPreserve all existing fetch and training register boundaries and latency.\nExtend the training event and row snapshot index to seven bits. Forward\nthe older event's complete post-update row only when its entire hashed\nindex matches the incoming event. This includes skipped allocations,\nreplacement, counter update and invalidation. Same row number in different\nbanks is independent. Commit one edge after accepted-MEM capture, exactly\nas today, sustaining one event per clock. Training proceeds across frontend\nholds; recovery preserves the resolving event and reset clears all bank\nvalidity and cancels pending training.\n\nKeep the three fixed fetch records and enqueue/dequeue schedule unchanged.\nCapture selected/target predictions with the exact accepted bus word and\nretain them through queue, decoded and EX holds. The actual successor and\nexisting accepted-MEM recovery remain authoritative for every instruction,\nincluding stale noncontrol entries, illegal instructions, misaligned\ntransfers and changed JALR targets. Preserve nret=1 external ports,\ndefault-illegal decoding, operand forwarding, blocking arithmetic,\nALTOPS behavior, contiguous RVFI order and exactly-once memory handshakes.\nRequire the unchanged formal, stalled ISS cosim and canonical CoreMark\nCRC/UART/marker/OOB gates. Judge median Gowin Fmax times bracketed\niterations/cycle; acceptance requires fitness above 233.61 iterations/sec.\n\nExploratory evidence: a fresh unmodified champion run reproduces exactly\n4,296,564 timed cycles. Straight expansion to an unbanked 128-row array\nuses 4,228,278 cycles but measures only 95.003 MHz median, insufficient for\nacceptance. Taken-only allocation with the original 32-entry organization\nuses 4,221,644 cycles. Both simulations complete with all canonical CRCs,\nsuccess UART, valid markers and no OOB. Correct-path replay estimates\n43,641 control-transfer misses for the proposed hashed 128-entry taken-only\npolicy versus the measured 73,619 in the champion. Replay ignores learning\nlatency and wrong-path fetch and is not a measured cycle or fitness gain.\nExplicit 32-row banking is essential because the unbanked capacity probe\ninferred extra BSRAM and exposed tag-read-to-valid-update timing paths.\nReproduce the proposed combined policy and measure its actual cycle count\nand median vendor timing; exploratory artifacts are not implementation\ninputs and do not establish tournament acceptance.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Implement four separate 32-row indexed BTB banks using the reversible\nseven-bit XOR index, full 23-bit tags and full aligned targets. Allocate\nconditional misses only when taken; preserve saturation on hits, strong\njump allocation and stale invalidation. Extend registered training and\nordered post-update forwarding with the complete hashed index, ensuring\nskipped allocations forward unchanged rows. Preserve fetch delivery,\ntraining latency, reset, prediction snapshots and recovery priority.\n'''\nd['changes'][1]['description']='''Extend the IF reference model to the reversible hashed index and exact\ntaken-only allocation policy. Assert that a not-taken miss preserves a\nconflicting valid entry, while a matching not-taken branch decrements its\ncounter. Cover four-bank independence, true full-tag replacement, adjacent\nsame-index updates and skipped allocations, saturation, high addresses,\naligned eligibility, reset cancellation and training on redirect. Retain\nall existing exact queue and immutable-snapshot assertions.\n'''\nd['changes'][2]['description']='''Exercise hot branches and jumps with repeated low PC offsets. Adapt\nonly predictor-specific table/index and allocation expectations to the\nnew policy, preserving exact RVFI successors, operands, traps, order,\nrecovery and transaction checks. Include both bus holds, blocking\ncompletion, changed JALR targets and stale predictions with no younger\nstores or retirement. Run the unchanged formal, ISS cosim, canonical\nCoreMark and median Gowin evaluation gates.\n'''\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_style=None,width=80))\nprint('Refined schema-valid hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_42", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Banked hashed BTB with taken-only allocation preserves useful targets'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 223.34 with 4,296,564 timed CoreMark cycles at\n95.961 MHz. Its 32-entry direct-mapped bimodal predictor produces 73,619\naccepted control-transfer recoveries in the measured interval: 55,992\nconditional branches, 15,638 direct jumps and 1,989 returns. Hot direct\njumps repeatedly miss, showing target conflicts rather than a return-stack\nopportunity. Every legal conditional branch currently allocates a row,\neven on a not-taken miss that needs no target, evicting useful taken paths.\nEarlier attempts mostly changed delivery or maintenance timing, and the\nchampion already has registered fetch and training boundaries. Focus this\nattempt solely on retaining useful predictor entries under conflicts.\n'''\nd['hypothesis']='''Replace the 32-entry tagged bimodal BTB with one conflict-resistant\n128-entry predictor: four indexed 32-entry banks, a reversible XOR index,\nand taken-only allocation on a tag miss. Compute the seven-bit index as\nPC[8:2] XOR PC[15:9], use index[6:5] as the bank and index[4:0] as its row,\nand retain the entire PC[31:9] tag and 30 aligned target bits. This is a\nfull tag: PC[15:9] is contained in the stored tag, so the tag and hashed\nindex uniquely reconstruct PC[31:2]. Do not use partial tags or shorten\ntargets. Mixing address bits disperses hot code with repeated low offsets;\ntaken-only allocation stops irrelevant not-taken misses from replacing\nuseful targets. These are one predictor-conflict policy, with no changes\nto frontend delivery, direction algorithm, recovery timing or execution.\n\nA matching legal conditional branch still updates its existing two-bit\ncounter for either outcome, using the current Boolean saturation equations.\nA conditional miss allocates weakly taken only when actually taken. A\nnot-taken conditional miss leaves the entire addressed row untouched:\nvalidity, tag, target and counter. Legal aligned JAL/JALR allocate or update\nstrongly taken as before. Ineligible events retain exact tag-qualified\nstale-entry invalidation, without erasing another PC's replacement. The\nallocation decision must gate both table writes and the logical post-update\nrow used for forwarding; merely suppressing the write while forwarding an\nimaginary allocation is incorrect.\n\nDeclare each bank's tag, target and counter arrays separately with 32 rows\ninside a constant-index generate block. Read each bank with the five-bit\nrow index, then select the bank with a balanced four-way selection. Keep\nindexed RAM-friendly storage, rather than parallel full-tag comparison\nagainst 128 flop words or a single dynamically indexed 128-row array.\nPreserve all existing fetch and training register boundaries and latency.\nExtend the training event and row snapshot index to seven bits. Forward\nthe older event's complete post-update row only when its entire hashed\nindex matches the incoming event. This includes skipped allocations,\nreplacement, counter update and invalidation. Same row number in different\nbanks is independent. Commit one edge after accepted-MEM capture, exactly\nas today, sustaining one event per clock. Training proceeds across frontend\nholds; recovery preserves the resolving event and reset clears all bank\nvalidity and cancels pending training.\n\nKeep the three fixed fetch records and enqueue/dequeue schedule unchanged.\nCapture selected/target predictions with the exact accepted bus word and\nretain them through queue, decoded and EX holds. The actual successor and\nexisting accepted-MEM recovery remain authoritative for every instruction,\nincluding stale noncontrol entries, illegal instructions, misaligned\ntransfers and changed JALR targets. Preserve nret=1 external ports,\ndefault-illegal decoding, operand forwarding, blocking arithmetic,\nALTOPS behavior, contiguous RVFI order and exactly-once memory handshakes.\nRequire the unchanged formal, stalled ISS cosim and canonical CoreMark\nCRC/UART/marker/OOB gates. Judge median Gowin Fmax times bracketed\niterations/cycle; acceptance requires fitness above 233.61 iterations/sec.\n\nExploratory evidence: a fresh unmodified champion run reproduces exactly\n4,296,564 timed cycles. Straight expansion to an unbanked 128-row array\nuses 4,228,278 cycles but measures only 95.003 MHz median, insufficient for\nacceptance. Taken-only allocation with the original 32-entry organization\nuses 4,221,644 cycles. Both simulations complete with all canonical CRCs,\nsuccess UART, valid markers and no OOB. Correct-path replay estimates\n43,641 control-transfer misses for the proposed hashed 128-entry taken-only\npolicy versus the measured 73,619 in the champion. Replay ignores learning\nlatency and wrong-path fetch and is not a measured cycle or fitness gain.\nExplicit 32-row banking is essential because the unbanked capacity probe\ninferred extra BSRAM and exposed tag-read-to-valid-update timing paths.\nReproduce the proposed combined policy and measure its actual cycle count\nand median vendor timing; exploratory artifacts are not implementation\ninputs and do not establish tournament acceptance.\n'''\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Implement four separate 32-row indexed BTB banks using the reversible\nseven-bit XOR index, full 23-bit tags and full aligned targets. Allocate\nconditional misses only when taken; preserve saturation on hits, strong\njump allocation and stale invalidation. Extend registered training and\nordered post-update forwarding with the complete hashed index, ensuring\nskipped allocations forward unchanged rows. Preserve fetch delivery,\ntraining latency, reset, prediction snapshots and recovery priority.\n'''\nd['changes'][1]['description']='''Extend the IF reference model to the reversible hashed index and exact\ntaken-only allocation policy. Assert that a not-taken miss preserves a\nconflicting valid entry, while a matching not-taken branch decrements its\ncounter. Cover four-bank independence, true full-tag replacement, adjacent\nsame-index updates and skipped allocations, saturation, high addresses,\naligned eligibility, reset cancellation and training on redirect. Retain\nall existing exact queue and immutable-snapshot assertions.\n'''\nd['changes'][2]['description']='''Exercise hot branches and jumps with repeated low PC offsets. Adapt\nonly predictor-specific table/index and allocation expectations to the\nnew policy, preserving exact RVFI successors, operands, traps, order,\nrecovery and transaction checks. Include both bus holds, blocking\ncompletion, changed JALR targets and stale predictions with no younger\nstores or retirement. Run the unchanged formal, ISS cosim, canonical\nCoreMark and median Gowin evaluation gates.\n'''\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_style=None,width=80))\nprint('Refined schema-valid hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Refined schema-valid hypothesis: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r12s2.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
