{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r13s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Cache local-history direction decisions beside the existing BTB\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's 32-entry target table still incurs 55,992 conditional\n  branch recoveries in the timed CoreMark interval. Expanding and hashing\n  the target table in r12s2 saved 3.09 percent of cycles but made fetch-PC\n  feedback the critical path and reduced Fmax to 85.308 MHz. Explore\n  conditional direction accuracy without increasing target lookup depth.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace each BTB row's single bimodal counter with a small private\n  two-level local direction predictor: three bits of resolved branch\n  history, eight two-bit saturating counters, and a cached prediction bit\n  for the current history. Fetch reads only this cached bit alongside the\n  existing valid/tag/target row. History selection and counter arithmetic\n  occur entirely behind the existing registered training ingress; never\n  add a history-to-counter lookup in the fetch-PC feedback path.\n\n  On an eligible matching conditional branch, update the counter selected\n  by its old resolved history, shift in the accepted outcome, and cache\n  the high bit of the counter selected by the resulting history. Include\n  the just-updated counter when the old and new histories coincide. On a\n  conditional tag miss, initialize all eight counters weakly toward the\n  first outcome, initialize history with that outcome, and cache the same\n  outcome. Jumps retain strongly taken prediction. Preserve the current\n  allocation policy, full tags, aligned targets, table size, indexed\n  storage, fixed fetch queue, recovery timing, and all top-level ports.\n\n  Extend the accepted-event row snapshot and complete post-update\n  forwarding to carry local history, every pattern counter, and cached\n  direction. Consecutive same-index events must observe replacements,\n  updates, and invalidations in order. Training still commits one edge\n  after accepted-MEM capture, including on redirects and during frontend\n  holds. Reset clears validity and ca\n…[1132 of 4204 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:87a902a59dfee000]…\nor\n      consecutive same-index events. Preserve all existing fetch and\n      training boundaries, full addresses, invalidation and recovery.\n  - file: test/test_if_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Extend the independent IF reference model with local histories,\n      all eight counter transitions, cached next-history decisions,\n      allocation initialization, jumps and tag-qualified invalidation.\n      Cover history self-transitions, consecutive collisions, high tags,\n      resets with pending training, recovery-edge training and holds.\n      Retain exact queue-order and immutable-prediction assertions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add repeating conditional patterns and loop exits under bus stalls.\n      Retain all architectural checks for RVFI operands/successors/order,\n      traps, immediate recovery, blocking completion, changed JALR\n      targets, stale entries and exactly-once stores. Adapt only explicit\n      predictor-state expectations to the documented direction policy.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
