{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print(d['id'],d['title'],'fitness=',d.get('fitness'),'cycles=',d.get('cycles'),'fmax=',d.get('fmax_mhz'))\n  if 'r12s2' in d['id'] or 'r11s2' in d['id'] or 'r7s2' in d['id']:\n   print(d['hypothesis'].get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(d.get('hypothesis'),dict) else d.get('hypothesis',''))\n   print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261002-003-r1s2 Small tagged bimodal predictor removes correctly predicted redirect bubbles fitness= 13.25 cycles= 4208674 fmax= 5.577\nhyp-20261002-003-r2s2 Timing-conscious tagged prediction on the multicycle-divider champion fitness= 113.27 cycles= 4208611 fmax= 47.673\nhyp-20261002-003-r3s2 Decouple predicted fetch with a compact four-entry flow-through queue fitness= 121.1 cycles= 3983322 fmax= 48.238\nhyp-20261002-003-r4s2 Buffer predicted fetch across the champion's execute holds fitness= 135.43 cycles= 4053425 fmax= 54.896\nhyp-20261002-003-r5s2 Register the predicted fetch stream without a dequeue-PC feedback path fitness= 152.34 cycles= 4141319 fmax= 63.09\nhyp-20261002-003-r6s2 Prequalify predictor recovery and pipeline resolved training events fitness= 167.56 cycles= 4409538 fmax= 73.885\nhyp-20261002-003-r7s2 Parallel BTB banks with local hysteresis and prequalified recovery fitness= 145.71 cycles= 4409538 fmax= 64.252\nImplement the existing 32-entry fully tagged bimodal BTB as 32 separately generated constant-index flop banks, with parallel tag comparison and balanced masked-OR target selection. The single angle is removing selected table-read and counter-update muxes from the predictor control cone. Keep the current prediction policy, direct combinational instruction delivery, immediate EX recovery, arithmetic latency and original once-per-EX-advance training latency. Do not add a FIFO, delayed training stage or another predictor algorithm.\n\nEach bank contains a resettable valid bit, full 25-bit PC[31:7] tag, aligned 30-bit target[31:2], and two direction-state flops. Decode fetch PC[6:2] against that bank's constant index in parallel with comparing its local tag to PC[31:7]. Its selected signal is fetch-row AND valid AND tag-match AND direction. Mask the bank's full aligned target by this selected signal. Combine all 32 masked targets and all selected bits through explicit five-level binary OR trees, like the existing register-file read tree. Select the reduced target when any selected bit is set,\n…[15331 of 18403 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6543c98da55bb06e]…\now array\nuses 4,228,278 cycles but measures only 95.003 MHz median, insufficient for\nacceptance. Taken-only allocation with the original 32-entry organization\nuses 4,221,644 cycles. Both simulations complete with all canonical CRCs,\nsuccess UART, valid markers and no OOB. Correct-path replay estimates\n43,641 control-transfer misses for the proposed hashed 128-entry taken-only\npolicy versus the measured 73,619 in the champion. Replay ignores learning\nlatency and wrong-path fetch and is not a measured cycle or fitness gain.\nExplicit 32-row banking is essential because the unbanked capacity probe\ninferred extra BSRAM and exposed tag-read-to-valid-update timing paths.\nReproduce the proposed combined policy and measure its actual cycle count\nand median vendor timing; exploratory artifacts are not implementation\ninputs and do not establish tournament acceptance.\n\nNOTES \nhyp-20261002-003-r13s2 Predict direct targets from instruction immediates with a direction-only table fitness= 219.09 cycles= 4153875 fmax= 91.007\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
