{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_39", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,135p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r14s2.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261002-003-r14s2\ntitle: \"Instruction-qualified compact signatures reduce target-predictor conflicts\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's 32-entry fully tagged BTB has 73,619 CoreMark control\n  recoveries in 4,296,564 timed cycles. Recent capacity/hash expansion\n  saved 3.09 percent of cycles but reduced median Gowin Fmax to 85.308\n  MHz; instruction-derived targets saved 3.32 percent but needed an IF\n  target adder and increased area. The existing precise successor check\n  already makes prediction aliases recoverable. Replacing full predictor\n  tags with two-bit signatures and qualifying predictions with the fetched\n  instruction can spend\n  storage on useful targets while shortening lookup and maintenance.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the fully tagged 32-entry BTB with a 128-entry compact-signature\n  target predictor qualified by the actual accepted instruction word.\n  Keep full aligned 30-bit targets, a two-bit signature PC[10:9], one\n  initialized bit and a two-bit saturating counter per row. Index both\n  fetch and training with PC[8:2] XOR PC[15:9].\n  Use one indexed target array, not a bank-selection hierarchy or a\n  parallel full-tag comparison tree. There is no IF target adder and no\n  instruction-word bypass into decode. This is one predictor organization\n  change; retain all pipeline, queue, recovery and arithmetic timing.\n\n  Predecode only legal conditional BRANCH funct3 values, JAL, and JALR\n  with funct3=0. A qualified control instruction selects the stored full\n  target only when the indexed row is initialized, its two-bit signature\n  matches, and counter[1] is set;\n  otherwise fetch PC+4. All other instructions predict PC+4 regardless of\n  predictor contents. Only an accepted enqueue snapshots this selection\n  and target and advances PC. Prediction metadata remains immutable with\n  its dynamic instruction through all queue and pipeline holds. Table\n  contents never certify instruction legality or architectural targets.\n\n  Train only legal aligned control transfers at the current \n…[3910 of 6982 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:596dff71bc4381cc]…\nit reset, Boolean\n      saturation, accepted training snapshots and ordered forwarding\n      of same-index post-update state. Preserve three fixed fetch\n      records, all queue enables and reset/recovery priorities.\n  - file: test/test_if_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Update the independent predictor model for intentional signature\n      aliasing, opcode/funct3 qualification, taken-only allocation,\n      unchanged targets on not-taken updates, all saturation transitions,\n      same-index delayed training and pending-reset cancellation. Keep\n      exact queue ordering and immutable prediction checks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add colliding legal control transfers with different full targets,\n      high-PC aliases, changed instruction words and JALR targets under\n      imem/dmem stalls. Verify precise recovery, full RVFI PCs and links,\n      strict order, alignment and illegal traps, wrong-path cancellation\n      and exactly-once stores without weakening existing assertions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom array import array\nfrom collections import Counter\nimport json\ntrace=array('I');trace.frombytes(open('/srv/hwebench/tmp/9d6f718c/bd97f927/r14s2/controls.bin','rb').read());events=list(zip(*[iter(trace)]*5))\nfor hb in (0,4,6,8,10):\n for db in (8,10):\n  rows=[None]*32;h=0;cs=[1]*(1<<db);misses=Counter()\n  for pc,insn,npc,target,marked in events:\n   op=insn&127;jump=op\"'!=99;taken=jump or npc!=pc+4;i=(pc>>2)&31;di=((pc>>2)''^h)&((1<<db)-1);row=rows[i];hit=row is not None and row[0]==pc\n   selected=hit and (jump or cs[di]>=2)\n   miss=selected!=taken or taken and (not hit or row[1]!=target)\n   if marked and miss:misses[op]+=1\n   if taken:rows[i]=(pc,target)\n   if not jump:\n    cs[di]=min(3,cs[di]+1) if taken else max(0,cs[di]-1);h=((h<<1)|taken)&((1<<hb)-1)\n  print(json.dumps({'\"'history_bits':hb,'direction_entries':1<<db,'misses':sum(misses.values()),'conditional':misses[99],'jal':misses[111],'jalr':misses[103]}))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
