edicted-fetch buffering saved\n  8.08% of those cycles, but achieved only 54.896 MHz and lost fitness.\n  Its measured worst path ended at u_if/dequeue_pc_q after traversing\n  forwarding and execute. Reconstructing buffered PCs from each consumed\n  prediction creates a second successor-selection register controlled by\n  backend acceptance. A registered queue of complete fe\n…[4546 of 7618 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:81a75fffb6f9c46d]…\nnd validate bounded lookahead.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Make IF's consumption hold depend on load-use, older memory holds,\n      and execute_busy rather than raw imemReady. Detect load-use from\n      the presented registered head. Preserve all existing flush/hold\n      priorities and retained MEM/WB forwarding behavior.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve existing tests and add registered-FIFO empty/refill,\n      pointer wrap, capacity, simultaneous push/pop, full-pop-without-push,\n      bus-stall consumption, and backend-hold filling cases. Check each\n      popped full PC and prediction snapshot against accepted bus work.\n      Exercise recovery/reset at all occupancies, stale BTB entries,\n      changed JALR targets, load-forwarded branches, blocking completions,\n      boundary lookahead, exact RVFI operands/order/traps, and exactly-once\n      stores. Require unchanged formal, stalled cosim, CRC/marker/UART\n      validation, and vendor timing gates.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
