se ineligible instruction.\nCorrect predictions allow the currently fetched successor to enter ID/EX\nwithout a bubble; all RVFI PC fields continue to report resolved values.\n\nA prediction changes the PC only on the edge that accepts its instruction\ninto ID/EX; load-use, imem, and dmem stalls prevent ordinary PC advance.\nAccept, hold, or clear prediction metadata together with its instruction,\nfollowing the existing stage enables and flush priorities. In particular,\nimem stalls still insert an invalid ID/EX bubble while older EX work may\nadvance, and load-use still inserts the existing bubble. Gate EX rec\n…[26413 of 29485 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:25ead6a1f24db1ca]…\n.\n\nThe bounded prototype's placement options [0, 1, 2] measure\n[61.323, 63.982, 63.982] MHz, with 4,236 LUT4, 1,164 FF, 76 LUT-RAM,\nsix BSRAMs and two DSPs. The unchanged CoreMark harness reports all\ncanonical CRCs, both timing markers, the required validation UART\nliteral, successful completion, and no OOB. Full RVFI ISS comparison\npasses selftest and all three random programs with zero waits and\nwith both random bus stalls, plus a directed JAL at 0x000ffffc that\nmust turn around without speculative access to 0x00100000: ten runs\ntotal. The probe is under cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe/\nregistered4_frontier and leaves champion RTL unchanged. Reimplement\nfrom this hypothesis and run all unchanged correctness/fitness gates;\nfull formal and directed FIFO/reset/stall validation remain required.\n\ncritical_path: {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -11.344, 'arrival_ns': 21.639, 'logic_cells': 22, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
