{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil,subprocess\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe/banked_v2').resolve();f=p/'formal_probe';d=f/'cores'/'benchprobe'\nfor sub in ['checks','insns']:\n shutil.copytree(Path('formal/riscv-formal')/sub,f/sub,dirs_exist_ok=True)\nshutil.copytree(p/'rtl',d,dirs_exist_ok=True);shutil.copyfile('formal/wrapper_si.sv',d/'wrapper.sv')\ns=Path('formal/checks_si.cfg').read_text().split('[verilog-files]')[0]\ns+='[verilog-files]\\\\n'+'\\\\n'.join('@basedir@/cores/@core@/'+q.name for q in [d/'core_pkg.sv']+sorted(q for q in d.glob('*.sv') if q.name\"'!='\"'core_pkg.sv'))+'\\\\n'\n(d/'checks.cfg').write_text(s)\nsubprocess.run(['python3','../../checks/genchecks.py'],cwd=d,check=True)\nPY\nmake -j8 -k -f makefile -C cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe/banked_v2/formal_probe/cores/benchprobe/checks > cores/bench/generated/hypothesis_probe/banked_v2/formal.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_27", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261002-003-r7s2.yaml');x=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nx['title']='Parallel BTB banks with local hysteresis and prequalified recovery'\nx['motivation']='''The champion scores 167.71 at 73.952 MHz with 4,409,538 timed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path crosses EX, IF and decode across 42 cells. The BTB uses dynamically indexed tags, targets and counters, serializing a table read before the tag comparison and feeding training through a selected counter read-modify-write. The prior registered-training proposal only moved the competing limit: an isolated rerun with decode-prequalified recovery on the latest champion reaches 72.840 MHz with unchanged cycles. Instead, represent the same predictor as independent flop entries, analogous to the separately generated flop-bank register file that improved round five, with parallel full-tag comparison and local two-bit state updates. This changes predictor hardware organization while retaining the proven prediction policy and learning latency.'''\nx['hypothesis']='''Implement the existing 32-entry fully tagged bimodal BTB as 32 separately generated constant-index flop banks, with parallel tag comparison and balanced masked-OR target selection. The single angle is removing selected table-read and counter-update muxes from the predictor control cone. Keep the current prediction policy, direct combinational instruction delivery, immediate EX recovery, arithmetic latency and original once-per-EX-advance training latency. Do not add a FIFO, delayed training stage or another predictor algorithm.\n\nEach bank contains a resettable valid bit, full 25-bit PC[31:7] tag, aligned 30-bit target[31:2], and two direction-state flops. Decode fetch PC[6:2] against that bank's constant index in parallel with comparing its local tag to PC[31:7]. Its selected signal is fetch-row AND valid AND tag-match AND direction. Mask the bank's full aligned target by this selected signal. Combine all 32 masked targets and all selected bits through explicit five-level binary OR trees, like the existing register-file read tree. Select the reduced target when any selected bit is set, otherwise PC+4. Distinct row selects guarantee at most one selected entry. Do not truncate high PC bits or use a partial tag. Store each word in a separate generated local register, so synthesis does not reconstruct dynamically indexed LUT-RAM read ports before tag comparison.\n\nEncode the saturating counter as direction D and strength S: strongly not taken=(0,1), weakly not taken=(0,0), weakly taken=(1,0), strongly taken=(1,1). On a matching conditional update with actual outcome T, assign D_next = S ? D : T and S_next = (D == T), using both OLD state bits. These equations implement exactly the existing two-bit saturation, including weak-state crossing and both bounds, without an adder, saturation comparator or dynamically selected old counter. On a tag miss allocate D=T,S=0; jumps allocate/update D=1,S=1. For each bank, decode train_pc[6:2] against its constant index and compare its local tag directly to train_pc[31:7]. Only the addressed bank consumes train_valid. Preserve aligned legal eligibility, full targets, tag-qualified noncontrol/ineligible invalidation, and updates exactly once per final EX advance. Reset clears every valid bit; unreset invalid tag/target/state payloads cannot select or affect training. Keep learning on the original update edge, without a live-training fetch bypass.\n\nPrequalify recovery in ID to keep the late forwarded comparison separate from static legality/target checks. Add prediction_wrong_taken, prediction_wrong_not_taken and prediction_train_eligible bits to ID/EX. Default both mismatch bits to the captured prediction_selected. For a validated aligned conditional branch, wrong_taken is \"'!prediction_selected OR direct_target != predicted_target, and wrong_not_taken is prediction_selected. For a validated aligned direct JAL both bits are !prediction_selected OR direct_target != predicted_target. Ordinary/illegal/misaligned direct instructions and JALR retain the default. Direct eligibility is a validated aligned branch or direct JAL. Capture, hold, clear and flush these bits with their instruction snapshot and keep operand refresh intact.\n\nFor nonpending EX, choose wrong_taken or wrong_not_taken directly with branch_cond; the bits agree for nonbranches. For pending completions default to the captured selected bit, and only a captured legal jump uses !pending_prediction_q OR captured_actual_target != pending_predicted_target_q. Preserve the existing JALR target capture, bit-zero clearing and misalignment trap, and MUL/DIV stale-prediction recovery only on completion. Keep redirect = existing train_valid AND prediction_wrong and all actual redirect_target/trap/link/RVFI calculations unchanged. Use the ID eligibility bit for fast direct training and a legal aligned captured jump for pending eligibility. This removes branch-dependent trap qualification from the local BTB write enable.\n\nMake raw fetch validity depend only on imem_ready. The existing redirect-driven ID/EX flush is authoritative cancellation of the younger fetch. Keep raw instruction, PC and prediction metadata independent of redirect. A redirect still overrides every ordinary PC hold, while ID/EX flush overrides a simultaneous younger load-use hold. EX still suppresses recovery behind older dmem or execute holds. This prevents redirect from reentering load-use detection through IF validity. Do not remove recovery gating from side effects, retirement or training. Selected stale predictions on ordinary, illegal, changed-target and misaligned instructions must recover before younger work executes.\n\nPreserve nret=1 and all external ports, full PC/target widths, decoder legality, RVFI operands and actual successors, contiguous order, arithmetic and ALTOPS behavior, held-operand refresh, load-use/bus semantics and exactly-once stores. Require unchanged unit, formal and stalled cosim/CoreMark gates. At unchanged cycles the acceptance threshold is median Gowin Fmax above approximately 77.354 MHz. The main risks are increased flop area, high PC/tag fanout, routing across the parallel entries, and a competing ALU critical path. Evaluate actual median vendor Fmax times bracketed iterations/cycle.'\"'''\nx['changes'][0]['description']='''Replace dynamic BTB arrays with independent generated valid/tag/target/direction/strength flop banks, local exact hysteresis updates and tag-qualified invalidation. Build balanced masked-OR lookup trees. Preserve original training edge, full tags/targets, PC hold/recovery priorities and change raw fetch validity to imemReady only.'''\nx['changes'][4]['description']='''Retain all existing assertions and add exact hysteresis transition/saturation, collision/replacement and stale-entry coverage. Exercise simultaneous stale-load recovery/load-use, imem/dmem holds, reset and blocking completion. Check correct predictions avoid bubbles, exact RVFI/order and exactly-once stores. No delayed-training timing adjustments are needed.'''\njsonschema.validate(x,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')));p.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=88))\nprint('Refined YAML schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
